I heard about the Wolf
Raiders on my radio.

518
00:19:33,273 --> 00:19:35,023
That's why I reacted.

519
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:37,577
- I think he's telling us the truth sir.

520
00:19:37,577 --> 00:19:38,626
- [Joel] I also believe in fairies.

521
00:19:38,626 --> 00:19:40,521
- I don't wanna get killed.

522
00:19:40,521 --> 00:19:42,852
- Captain, UFOs on our radar screen.

523
00:19:42,852 --> 00:19:45,003
- [Crow] I'm busy can't ya see?

524
00:19:45,003 --> 00:19:46,035
Check it.

525
00:19:46,035 --> 00:19:47,359
- Yes sir.

526
00:19:47,359 --> 00:19:48,192
Let's go.

527
00:19:48,192 --> 00:19:49,025
- Right.

528
00:19:49,025 --> 00:19:50,192
- [Tom] Right!

529
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,233
- Nice cuff links.

530
00:19:55,233 --> 00:19:57,150
- [Joel] Pierre Cardin.

531
00:19:58,325 --> 00:20:01,043
Now we're gonna spank you big time.

532
00:20:01,043 --> 00:20:03,152
- I don't want you to move from this spot.

533
00:20:03,152 --> 00:20:05,398
Unless of course you feel
like leaving this ship

534
00:20:05,398 --> 00:20:07,231
and floating in space.

535
00:20:09,548 --> 00:20:11,555
- [Crow] You can get up now.

536
00:20:11,555 --> 00:20:15,987
- [Joel] My sleeve's
comfortable but jeepers.

537
00:20:15,987 --> 00:20:16,820
Huh?

538
00:20:19,632 --> 00:20:21,806
(beeping)

539
00:20:21,806 --> 00:20:24,660
- [Tom] Hey, look that
truck's headed to Utah.

540
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:25,655
- You keep your eyes on the screen.

541
00:20:25,655 --> 00:20:26,488
- Yes sir.

542
00:20:27,707 --> 00:20:28,846
- All instruments operational?

543
00:20:28,846 --> 00:20:29,679
- Yes sir.

544
00:20:29,679 --> 00:20:31,351
- [Crow] And how.

545
00:20:31,351 --> 00:20:33,866
- We're approaching route MMS 600, sir.

546
00:20:33,866 --> 00:20:36,586
- [Joel] And my heart is racing.

547
00:20:36,586 --> 00:20:38,349
- Look how fast they're going.

548
00:20:38,349 --> 00:20:39,675
Who can generate that kind of velocity?

549
00:20:39,675 --> 00:20:41,419
- Wolf Raiders
- [Tom] I can.

550
00:20:41,419 --> 00:20:42,648
For sure.

551
00:20:42,648 --> 00:20:43,481
(sniffing)

552
00:20:43,481 --> 00:20:44,314
- [Crow] You smell good.

553
00:20:44,314 --> 00:20:48,685
- Sir I don't think
we're any match for them.

554
00:20:48,685 --> 00:20:49,792
- [Crow] Got my nose.

555
00:20:49,792 --> 00:20:50,676
- Look at that!

556
00:20:50,676 --> 00:20:51,710
(mumbling)

557
00:20:51,710 --> 00:20:55,097
- You can't take them on
in this beat up old crate.

558
00:20:55,097 --> 00:20:55,993
Change course.

559
00:20:55,993 --> 00:20:57,397
- Someone put a gag in his mouth.

560
00:20:57,397 --> 00:20:59,980
- [All] I'll do it, I'll do it.

561
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:04,555
- He's talking sense for once.

562
00:21:04,555 --> 00:21:06,849
They have greater firing power.

563
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:09,451
This ship is much too old
to take on superior forces

564
00:21:09,451 --> 00:21:10,852
like Wolf Raiders.
(Tom clucking)

565
00:21:10,852 --> 00:21:12,120
- It's too late to turn around now.

566
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:15,702
I think they've spotted our position.

567
00:21:15,702 --> 00:21:17,702
- [Crow] They're Batman.

568
00:21:19,383 --> 00:21:20,699
- [Joel] Are they listening to ELO?

569
00:21:20,699 --> 00:21:21,532
- Here they come.

570
00:21:21,532 --> 00:21:23,865
(whooshing)

571
00:21:25,682 --> 00:21:28,648
- [Crow] You can see the drapery hooks.

572
00:21:28,648 --> 00:21:29,664
(beeping)

573
00:21:29,664 --> 00:21:31,703
- [Joel] Are you a good
witch or a bad witch?

574
00:21:31,703 --> 00:21:32,536
- This is it.

575
00:21:32,536 --> 00:21:33,369
- [Tom] Let's go.

576
00:21:33,369 --> 00:21:34,202
Hey a got an idea.

577
00:21:34,202 --> 00:21:35,813
Let's get that box of
hats out of the back.

578
00:21:35,813 --> 00:21:39,646
- [Crow] Oh I know where
that is, I'll get it.

579
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:45,570
(doors slamming)

580
00:21:51,908 --> 00:21:54,822
- What are you two yard monkeys doin' now?

581
00:21:54,822 --> 00:21:57,685
- Well seein' the stupid
Wolf Raider hair helmets

582
00:21:57,685 --> 00:21:58,880
in the experiment reminded me

583
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:01,130
of all this stuff from
the last hat party we had.

584
00:22:01,130 --> 00:22:02,199
Hey, put that one on.

585
00:22:02,199 --> 00:22:03,120
- Yeah.

586
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:04,902
- Oh no I don't wanna.

587
00:22:04,902 --> 00:22:06,090
I'd feel silly.

588
00:22:06,090 --> 00:22:07,061
- I remember that one.

589
00:22:07,061 --> 00:22:08,863
That one was the grandest of all.

590
00:22:08,863 --> 00:22:10,531
- Yeah, yeah, I thought we could take some

591
00:22:10,531 --> 00:22:12,025
of these and have fun with them

592
00:22:12,025 --> 00:22:14,012
and maybe make up even more stupider hats.

593
00:22:14,012 --> 00:22:15,173
Ya know, for the next party.

594
00:22:15,173 --> 00:22:16,141
- Oh say, put that one on me.

595
00:22:16,141 --> 00:22:17,089
I got an idea here.

596
00:22:17,089 --> 00:22:17,922
- Okay.

597
00:22:17,922 --> 00:22:19,438
- [Tom] Now ya see this is a helmet

598
00:22:19,438 --> 00:22:21,320
for astronauts who are losing their hair.

599
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:22,153
(Crow laughs)

600
00:22:22,153 --> 00:22:23,026
When you see Mr. Balding call him over.

601
00:22:23,026 --> 00:22:23,859
- That's a good idea.

602
00:22:23,859 --> 00:22:25,334
- Okay, all right, I'm into it now.

603
00:22:25,334 --> 00:22:26,700
Look at this one.

604
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:28,684
This goes back to 1981.

605
00:22:28,684 --> 00:22:30,487
I'm a punk from space, get it?

606
00:22:30,487 --> 00:22:31,320
- Ooh.

607
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:34,048
♫ I am an anarchist ♫

608
00:22:34,048 --> 00:22:34,881
- Get it?

609
00:22:34,881 --> 00:22:36,232
- This big one over here.

610
00:22:36,232 --> 00:22:37,065
Put this one one me, Joel.

611
00:22:37,065 --> 00:22:37,898
- Okay.

612
00:22:37,898 --> 00:22:39,278
- Now I got, I got it.

613
00:22:39,278 --> 00:22:40,849
This is what Patti Labelle would look like

614
00:22:40,849 --> 00:22:42,050
on the space shuttle.

615
00:22:42,050 --> 00:22:42,883
Wahhhhhhh!

616
00:22:45,285 --> 00:22:46,263
- Wow that's cool.

617
00:22:46,263 --> 00:22:47,096
- Go ahead, try that other one there.

618
00:22:47,096 --> 00:22:47,929
Okay.

619
00:22:47,929 --> 00:22:48,762
- Yeah, where is it?

620
00:22:48,762 --> 00:22:49,595
Oh way down there.

621
00:22:49,595 --> 00:22:50,428
- Oh, oh, watch the hand.

622
00:22:50,428 --> 00:22:51,261
- Sorry yeah.

623
00:22:51,261 --> 00:22:52,094
- Oh wow look it.

624
00:22:52,094 --> 00:22:53,904
It's the Ted Koppel satellite of hair.

625
00:22:53,904 --> 00:22:55,915
- Or you can pull down the curl in front

626
00:22:55,915 --> 00:22:57,915
and it would look just
like Frank's hair helmet.

627
00:22:57,915 --> 00:22:58,748
(Crow laughs)

628
00:22:58,748 --> 00:23:02,317
- Oh I think those things are wonderful.

629
00:23:02,317 --> 00:23:04,266
(all laughing)

630
00:23:04,266 --> 00:23:06,869
- Push the button, Frank.

631
00:23:06,869 --> 00:23:08,998
- Doctor F you better
come have a look at this.

632
00:23:08,998 --> 00:23:10,815
Joel and the bots are
making fun of my hair.

633
00:23:10,815 --> 00:23:12,382
My hair!

634
00:23:12,382 --> 00:23:14,568
- Now Frank, let them
have their little fun.

635
00:23:14,568 --> 00:23:16,627
The experiment's not quite over

636
00:23:16,627 --> 00:23:18,279
and they'll soon live to regret it.

637
00:23:18,279 --> 00:23:20,640
(all laughing)

638
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,648
- Wait hey guys, look at this one, hey.

639
00:23:22,648 --> 00:23:23,796
(grunting)

640
00:23:23,796 --> 00:23:24,910
This one looks like Doctor Forrester

641
00:23:24,910 --> 00:23:27,162
if his head got sucked
into the vacuum of space

642
00:23:27,162 --> 00:23:28,279
through a keyhole.

643
00:23:28,279 --> 00:23:29,381
(all laugh)

644
00:23:29,381 --> 00:23:30,417
- Now you cut that out.

645
00:23:30,417 --> 00:23:32,150
Remember what I said about hat parties.

646
00:23:32,150 --> 00:23:33,091
You get your little hinders back

647
00:23:33,091 --> 00:23:35,162
into that theater and you watch the film.

648
00:23:35,162 --> 00:23:37,190
And I'm not amused by
your antics in the least.

649
00:23:37,190 --> 00:23:39,208
- I thought it was a sheer delight.

650
00:23:39,208 --> 00:23:42,522
I think that's about as
grand as a hat party can get.

651
00:23:42,522 --> 00:23:43,355
(buzzing)

652
00:23:43,355 --> 00:23:45,921
(moaning)

653
00:23:45,921 --> 00:23:48,039
That was about as painful as a cattle prod

654
00:23:48,039 --> 00:23:49,284
to the shoulder could get.

655
00:23:49,284 --> 00:23:51,538
(buzzing)

656
00:23:51,538 --> 00:23:53,418
- Send him commercial, Frank.

657
00:23:53,418 --> 00:23:55,332
- I'll send him commercial sign.

658
00:23:55,332 --> 00:23:56,866
- [Jack] But later on in the program,

659
00:23:56,866 --> 00:23:58,391
Linda Ellerbee will be out.

660
00:23:58,391 --> 00:24:00,217
(buzzing)
(moaning)

661
00:24:00,217 --> 00:24:02,800
(lively music)

662
00:24:08,032 --> 00:24:09,357
- [Joe] I hate to say it but Jack Perkins

663
00:24:09,357 --> 00:24:10,300
had that comin'.

664
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:11,246
- [Tom] Yep.
- Oh yeah.

665
00:24:11,246 --> 00:24:12,249
Poor guy.

666
00:24:12,249 --> 00:24:15,749
- That party never ended like that before.

667
00:24:19,676 --> 00:24:20,509
(engines roaring)

668
00:24:20,509 --> 00:24:21,676
- [Tom] Ooooh.

669
00:24:23,513 --> 00:24:25,250
(coughing)

670
00:24:25,250 --> 00:24:27,167
- [Crow] I'm exhausted.

671
00:24:28,466 --> 00:24:29,399
- [Joel] I wish someone would turn off

672
00:24:29,399 --> 00:24:31,482
the courageous cat music.

673
00:24:33,289 --> 00:24:36,122
- [Tom] Chili peppers burn my gut.

674
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:39,997
Doom, doom, doom, doom.

675
00:24:46,250 --> 00:24:47,083
- [Crow] Oop, chin rascal.

676
00:24:47,083 --> 00:24:49,581
- [Tom] More like face rascal.

677
00:24:49,581 --> 00:24:51,331
- [Crow] Space speed.

678
00:24:53,754 --> 00:24:55,787
- [Joel] Edward Munch I presume?

679
00:24:55,787 --> 00:24:57,489
- [Tom] Ho ho, look at that.

680
00:24:57,489 --> 00:24:59,522
- [Joel] Giving him a face massage.

681
00:24:59,522 --> 00:25:00,866
- [Crow] Well we can't
fight 'em but we can confuse

682
00:25:00,866 --> 00:25:02,460
the heck out of 'em.

683
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:05,210
(dramatic music)

684
00:25:08,728 --> 00:25:10,626
Fries are up.

685
00:25:10,626 --> 00:25:11,631
- [Tom] Yep.

686
00:25:11,631 --> 00:25:14,413
(beeping)

687
00:25:14,413 --> 00:25:16,459
- [Joel] Whoa that was us.

688
00:25:16,459 --> 00:25:17,292
Jeepers.

689
00:25:22,482 --> 00:25:25,399
- [Tom] Somebody hang up the phone.

690
00:25:27,286 --> 00:25:29,055
Now watch out for that, ugh!

691
00:25:29,055 --> 00:25:29,888
Well, never mind.

692
00:25:29,888 --> 00:25:31,055
- [Crow] Oops.

693
00:25:32,530 --> 00:25:33,613
- Cease fire.

694
00:25:38,048 --> 00:25:41,908
Bacchus 3, you haven't
seen the last of me.

695
00:25:41,908 --> 00:25:43,565
- [Crow] Jim Backus?

696
00:25:43,565 --> 00:25:45,330
(beeping)

697
00:25:45,330 --> 00:25:48,163
- [Joel] Uh, cookies are done sir.

698
00:25:55,298 --> 00:25:56,438
- [Tom] Cooh huh?

699
00:25:56,438 --> 00:25:57,271
- [Joel] Yeah.

700
00:25:57,271 --> 00:25:59,740
- Looks like we made it.

701
00:25:59,740 --> 00:26:01,956
- [Tom] Left each other
all the way into a knuckle.

702
00:26:01,956 --> 00:26:05,039
- That's for knockin' out my officer.

703
00:26:07,192 --> 00:26:08,243
Look alive, you guys.

704
00:26:08,243 --> 00:26:09,177
There's work to do.

705
00:26:09,177 --> 00:26:10,866
- [Tom] I'm alive, sir.

706
00:26:10,866 --> 00:26:12,629
- [Crow] I'm sorry honey.

707
00:26:12,629 --> 00:26:13,462
Are you okay?

708
00:26:13,462 --> 00:26:14,600
- [Joe] Rocky, are you okay?

709
00:26:14,600 --> 00:26:15,659
- [Joe] Say something.

710
00:26:15,659 --> 00:26:18,325
- [Tom] Yo Adrian, uh, cut me, cut me.

711
00:26:18,325 --> 00:26:20,041
- We did it, we got away from them.

712
00:26:20,041 --> 00:26:21,158
- [Joel] I did?

713
00:26:21,158 --> 00:26:23,161
Yeah I did, huh huh.

714
00:26:23,161 --> 00:26:25,010
- Who is this guy?

715
00:26:25,010 --> 00:26:27,440
- All I know is he's ten
times as strong as we are.

716
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:28,291
- [Tom] And I love him.

717
00:26:28,291 --> 00:26:30,008
- [Joe] And he got us
through the Wolf Raiders.

718
00:26:30,008 --> 00:26:33,591
- [Tom] A snappy dresser
and a good friend.

719
00:26:34,514 --> 00:26:37,764
Hey bookmobile, summer reading program.

720
00:26:40,520 --> 00:26:44,513
- [Crow] Third planet from the
sun will be known as Earth.

721
00:26:44,513 --> 00:26:45,513
Pretty much.

722
00:26:47,142 --> 00:26:48,779
- [Tom] Oh no, we'll
have to circle LaGuardia

723
00:26:48,779 --> 00:26:50,320
for an hour I'm bettin'.

724
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:53,711
- [Joel] Hey I can see the Great Wall.

725
00:26:53,711 --> 00:26:55,294
- [Crow] It's okay.

726
00:26:57,477 --> 00:26:59,727
- [Tom] Do do do, do do do.

727
00:27:00,867 --> 00:27:02,750
- [Crow] They're goin' to the Dells.

728
00:27:02,750 --> 00:27:05,609
(dramatic music)

729
00:27:05,609 --> 00:27:07,258
- [Joel] Uh, Jimmy left his Legos

730
00:27:07,258 --> 00:27:09,491
in the driveway again.

731
00:27:09,491 --> 00:27:10,908
- [Tom] That kid.

732
00:27:13,774 --> 00:27:16,923
Ya know, I tell ya, that
ship is burping out a lot

733
00:27:16,923 --> 00:27:18,545
of chlorofluorocarbons there.

734
00:27:18,545 --> 00:27:21,621
Punchin' a hole in the ozone.

735
00:27:21,621 --> 00:27:23,393
(Crow coughs)

736
00:27:23,393 --> 00:27:27,724
- [Joel] The bank will be
closing in five minutes.

737
00:27:27,724 --> 00:27:29,427
- [Voiceover] Here is the
latest report on the attack

738
00:27:29,427 --> 00:27:30,907
on the Valna Raiders.

739
00:27:30,907 --> 00:27:33,449
Due to heavy damage,
aerospace port number six

740
00:27:33,449 --> 00:27:36,123
has been closed to all
traffic until further notice.

741
00:27:36,123 --> 00:27:37,623
- That's our port.

742
00:27:38,622 --> 00:27:40,097
- [Man] What'll we do?

743
00:27:40,097 --> 00:27:41,382
- I just talked to headquarters.

744
00:27:41,382 --> 00:27:43,165
They said all streets leaving the base

745
00:27:43,165 --> 00:27:44,832
have been destroyed.

746
00:27:45,885 --> 00:27:46,905
- Check that out.

747
00:27:46,905 --> 00:27:47,829
- [Tom] Check her out.

748
00:27:47,829 --> 00:27:48,662
- Heyyyy.

749
00:27:50,228 --> 00:27:52,142
- [Voiceover] Attention please.

750
00:27:52,142 --> 00:27:53,012
- Take charge of the prisoner.

751
00:27:53,012 --> 00:27:54,094
- Yes, sir.

752
00:27:54,094 --> 00:27:55,265
- [Voiceover] Flights are kindly requested

753
00:27:55,265 --> 00:27:58,117
to proceed immediately to
Space Command headquarters

754
00:27:58,117 --> 00:27:59,529
for debriefing.

755
00:27:59,529 --> 00:28:02,514
We repeat, senior officers
of all incoming flights

756
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:06,718
proceed at once to Space
Command headquarters.

757
00:28:06,718 --> 00:28:10,631
- [Crow] Watch the steno
pool go wild for his vinyl.

758
00:28:10,631 --> 00:28:12,948
- 'Scuse me, how can I
contact space port six?

759
00:28:12,948 --> 00:28:13,859
- Right up there, sir.

760
00:28:13,859 --> 00:28:15,067
- Thank you.

761
00:28:15,067 --> 00:28:17,763
- [Tom] I just wanna check
out my car loan here.

762
00:28:17,763 --> 00:28:19,811
Get out of my way.

763
00:28:19,811 --> 00:28:20,841
(beeping)

764
00:28:20,841 --> 00:28:21,674
- [Crow] Alt function.

765
00:28:21,674 --> 00:28:22,674
- [Tom] Huh?

766
00:28:26,670 --> 00:28:28,137
- [Joel] Noah's Ark?

767
00:28:28,137 --> 00:28:30,637
- Hey and there's Moses' Jeep.

768
00:28:31,511 --> 00:28:33,658
(Tom laughs)

769
00:28:33,658 --> 00:28:35,293
- [Tom] Ewwww.

770
00:28:35,293 --> 00:28:37,202
- Did he tell you how he got that wound?

771
00:28:37,202 --> 00:28:38,035
- [Crow] I gave it to him.

772
00:28:38,035 --> 00:28:40,911
- He refused to answer
any of our questions.

773
00:28:40,911 --> 00:28:43,282
He started shouting and acting crazy.

774
00:28:43,282 --> 00:28:45,507
So I gave him a tranquilizer to quiet him.

775
00:28:45,507 --> 00:28:46,920
- Is he likely to get violent?

776
00:28:46,920 --> 00:28:48,211
- He's highly unpredictable.

777
00:28:48,211 --> 00:28:49,921
Please maintain him
here under heavy guard.

778
00:28:49,921 --> 00:28:50,754
- Thanks for the warning.

779
00:28:50,754 --> 00:28:51,587
- Good-bye.

780
00:28:51,587 --> 00:28:52,420
Come on.

781
00:28:54,970 --> 00:28:57,584
- [Tom] Everybody's doing
their banking in this movie.

782
00:28:57,584 --> 00:28:58,974
- [Joel] Looks like Ken's driving

783
00:28:58,974 --> 00:29:01,391
the Malibu Barbie beach jeep.

784
00:29:02,348 --> 00:29:05,063
- [Tom] I just have to get out
some money for the weekend.

785
00:29:05,063 --> 00:29:07,039
Aww dang, they're closed.

786
00:29:07,039 --> 00:29:10,414
Boy I would love to be a banker.

787
00:29:10,414 --> 00:29:11,700
- [Joel] So uh, dinner Thursday?

788
00:29:11,700 --> 00:29:13,082
Great.

789
00:29:13,082 --> 00:29:15,232
- [Tom] Get out of my way.

790
00:29:15,232 --> 00:29:16,372
Hi say, dinner Friday?

791
00:29:16,372 --> 00:29:17,372
Great, okay.

792
00:29:26,005 --> 00:29:27,733
- [Crow] Oh hi, dinner Sunday?

793
00:29:27,733 --> 00:29:29,033
Can we do it?

794
00:29:29,033 --> 00:29:30,283
Oh you're free.

795
00:29:33,773 --> 00:29:36,982
- [Joel] Ladies and
gentlemen, this is Elvis.

796
00:29:36,982 --> 00:29:39,890
- [Crow] Thank you, thank you very much.

797
00:29:39,890 --> 00:29:41,806
- [Tom] The audience has left the arena.

798
00:29:41,806 --> 00:29:44,968
(Joel laughs)

799
00:29:44,968 --> 00:29:46,130
- [Joel] What the?

800
00:29:46,130 --> 00:29:46,963
Oh huh?

801
00:29:48,382 --> 00:29:51,268
- [Tom] Baby doll, ballet slippers.

802
00:29:51,268 --> 00:29:52,200
Huh?

803
00:29:52,200 --> 00:29:53,867
A geometric nucleus?

804
00:29:55,457 --> 00:29:56,707
And a chew toy.

805
00:29:58,153 --> 00:30:02,320
- [Crow] Well I'll just
rifle the dead's stuff here.

806
00:30:04,997 --> 00:30:06,196
- [Joel] So dinner Sunday?

807
00:30:06,196 --> 00:30:07,279
- [All] D'oh!

808
00:30:08,529 --> 00:30:10,196
- [Tom] What a gaff.

809
00:30:14,276 --> 00:30:15,334
- Maryanne?

810
00:30:15,334 --> 00:30:18,834
- [Tom] Ginger, Skipper, Lovey, Professor.

811
00:30:22,309 --> 00:30:25,977
- [Crow] Thank you, thank you very much.

812
00:30:25,977 --> 00:30:26,810
- Barbara?

813
00:30:26,810 --> 00:30:28,008
- [Joel] Did he say Whopper?

814
00:30:28,008 --> 00:30:30,891
- [Tom] Sounded like Whopper.

815
00:30:30,891 --> 00:30:31,974
- Oh darling!

816
00:30:33,642 --> 00:30:35,846
Where's Maryanne?

817
00:30:35,846 --> 00:30:38,578
- [Crow] Uh dead, uh dusting downstairs.

818
00:30:38,578 --> 00:30:41,269
- [Barbara] Where is she?

819
00:30:41,269 --> 00:30:43,655
- Maryanne's resting.

820
00:30:43,655 --> 00:30:44,488
- [Crow] In peace.

821
00:30:44,488 --> 00:30:46,456
- [Tom] Pieces.

822
00:30:46,456 --> 00:30:49,474
- Oh my goodness, I was
so worried something

823
00:30:49,474 --> 00:30:51,903
had happened to her in
that terrible attack.

824
00:30:51,903 --> 00:30:52,799
- [Tom] Yeah whatever.

825
00:30:52,799 --> 00:30:54,641
- I couldn't find her anywhere.

826
00:30:54,641 --> 00:30:56,007
Then I passed out.

827
00:30:56,007 --> 00:30:57,302
And woke up here.

828
00:30:57,302 --> 00:30:58,135
- [Tom] What'd ya say?

829
00:30:58,135 --> 00:30:58,968
What a view.

830
00:30:58,968 --> 00:30:59,801
You got a great room here.

831
00:30:59,801 --> 00:31:02,638
- [Barbara] Now we're all together again.

832
00:31:02,638 --> 00:31:05,276
(gasps)

833
00:31:05,276 --> 00:31:07,794
(ominous music)

834
00:31:07,794 --> 00:31:10,139
- [Joel] Well, that does
take the pressure off.

835
00:31:10,139 --> 00:31:11,207
- [Tom] Yeah.

836
00:31:11,207 --> 00:31:14,371
(dramatic music)

837
00:31:14,371 --> 00:31:16,435
- [Crow] Hey, Ken's got a problem.

838
00:31:16,435 --> 00:31:18,117
Ken wasn't careful.

839
00:31:18,117 --> 00:31:20,200
Ken's going to get candy.

840
00:31:21,987 --> 00:31:23,083
- Oh no you don't.

841
00:31:23,083 --> 00:31:23,966
- Please sir, you mustn't.

842
00:31:23,966 --> 00:31:25,055
- [Tom] Oh yes I do.

843
00:31:25,055 --> 00:31:25,888
(laughs)

844
00:31:25,888 --> 00:31:27,506
Physician heal thyself.

845
00:31:27,506 --> 00:31:30,846
(ominous music)

846
00:31:30,846 --> 00:31:32,199
- [Joel] I know just what to do.

847
00:31:32,199 --> 00:31:35,233
I'll sneak out of here
disguised as Chad Everett.

848
00:31:35,233 --> 00:31:37,400
- [Tom] That always works.

849
00:31:40,263 --> 00:31:43,013
- [Crow] Hey, McGarret's up here.

850
00:31:46,014 --> 00:31:49,750
- [Tom] Ooh, Tuckskins in
husky, slim and regular.

851
00:31:49,750 --> 00:31:51,579
- [Joel] Ken's out cross-training.

852
00:31:51,579 --> 00:31:53,213
Just do it.

853
00:31:53,213 --> 00:31:55,463
- [Voiceover] Ken was safe for the moment

854
00:31:55,463 --> 00:31:56,995
but where could he go?

855
00:31:56,995 --> 00:31:58,778
What could he do?

856
00:31:58,778 --> 00:32:01,410
Outcast on his own planet.

857
00:32:01,410 --> 00:32:03,350
A fugitive alien on earth.

858
00:32:03,350 --> 00:32:06,275
He'd have to make a fresh start somewhere.

859
00:32:06,275 --> 00:32:07,475
- [Crow] In the robot holocaust.

860
00:32:07,475 --> 00:32:08,457
- [Voiceover] Where?

861
00:32:08,457 --> 00:32:09,943
And how could he get there?

862
00:32:09,943 --> 00:32:13,558
- [Crow] And what of Bob's love for Chad?

863
00:32:13,558 --> 00:32:14,952
(explosion)

864
00:32:14,952 --> 00:32:16,401
- [Tom] Uh sorry, that was me.

865
00:32:16,401 --> 00:32:17,738
Excuse me.

866
00:32:17,738 --> 00:32:19,318
- [Voiceover] A spacecraft.

867
00:32:19,318 --> 00:32:20,351
- [Joel] Duh.

868
00:32:20,351 --> 00:32:21,934
- I'll have to hijack one.

869
00:32:21,934 --> 00:32:22,928
- [Joel] Ho ho, better.

870
00:32:22,928 --> 00:32:25,345
- [Crow] Not in those slacks.

871
00:32:31,548 --> 00:32:33,387
- [Joel] Now, now, I cue myself, jump back

872
00:32:33,387 --> 00:32:36,537
and ha, jumping, running and spinning.

873
00:32:36,537 --> 00:32:37,514
- [Tom] Follow me.

874
00:32:37,514 --> 00:32:39,014
Oh, I'm over here.

875
00:32:41,925 --> 00:32:42,758
Careful.

876
00:32:46,254 --> 00:32:47,538
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight,

877
00:32:47,538 --> 00:32:48,539
nine, ten, eleven, twelve,
thirteen, fourteen,

878
00:32:48,539 --> 00:32:49,925
fifteen, sixteen, seventeen.

879
00:32:49,925 --> 00:32:51,661
(panting)

880
00:32:51,661 --> 00:32:53,529
- [Joel] This is good for the glutes.

881
00:32:53,529 --> 00:32:54,918
Push, push guys.

882
00:32:54,918 --> 00:32:56,421
- [Tom] The burn, the burn.

883
00:32:56,421 --> 00:32:58,588
(panting)

884
00:33:01,146 --> 00:33:04,459
- [Joel] He's at a ski
lodge now, what gives?

885
00:33:04,459 --> 00:33:06,117
- [Tom] Excuse me, can you tell me where

886
00:33:06,117 --> 00:33:07,804
I could hijack a spaceship anybody?

887
00:33:07,804 --> 00:33:09,137
Okay never mind.

888
00:33:10,151 --> 00:33:12,605
Anybody, uh spaceship?

889
00:33:12,605 --> 00:33:15,022
I need to hijack a spaceship.

890
00:33:16,566 --> 00:33:17,399
Say!

891
00:33:18,357 --> 00:33:19,557
- [Ken] Nobody around.

892
00:33:19,557 --> 00:33:21,674
But how do I get aboard?

893
00:33:21,674 --> 00:33:22,964
- [Tom] Go through the lumber yard.

894
00:33:22,964 --> 00:33:24,140
That's how you get a board.

895
00:33:24,140 --> 00:33:25,973
Get it, I said lumber.

896
00:33:27,108 --> 00:33:28,147
- Hello, stranger.

897
00:33:28,147 --> 00:33:29,690
- [Crow] Hi, sailor.

898
00:33:29,690 --> 00:33:31,121
- Did you just drop by for coffee

899
00:33:31,121 --> 00:33:32,187
or are were you planning to stay on

900
00:33:32,187 --> 00:33:33,339
for the cocktail hour?

901
00:33:33,339 --> 00:33:34,172
(gun cocks)

902
00:33:34,172 --> 00:33:36,687
(gun fires)

903
00:33:36,687 --> 00:33:40,119
- [Crow] I'll have that cocktail now.

904
00:33:40,119 --> 00:33:43,318
- Well friend, not a very gracious guest.

905
00:33:43,318 --> 00:33:44,545
- [Crow] I've brought crackers.

906
00:33:44,545 --> 00:33:46,062
- It isn't very courteous to point a gun.

907
00:33:46,062 --> 00:33:48,449
- [Joel] It's not courteous
to point your finger, Gold.

908
00:33:48,449 --> 00:33:49,282
- You shouldn't have run away

909
00:33:49,282 --> 00:33:51,427
from that nice clean infirmary.

910
00:33:51,427 --> 00:33:52,500
Now how about.
- [Tom] St. James infirmary.

911
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:53,550
Giving me the gun?

912
00:33:53,550 --> 00:33:55,027
- That's enough.

913
00:33:55,027 --> 00:33:56,516
Turn around and face the wall.

914
00:33:56,516 --> 00:33:57,349
- [Joel] The wall?

915
00:33:57,349 --> 00:33:58,182
- Go on.

916
00:33:58,182 --> 00:34:00,660
(Joe laughs)

917
00:34:00,660 --> 00:34:01,593
Don't you think it'd be a good idea

918
00:34:01,593 --> 00:34:02,458
to check if it's loaded?

919
00:34:02,458 --> 00:34:03,291
- What?

920
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:04,124
- [All] Huh?

921
00:34:04,124 --> 00:34:05,624
- [Crow] Room 235.

922
00:34:06,537 --> 00:34:07,860
- [Joel] Works every time.

923
00:34:07,860 --> 00:34:09,320
- Stupidest thing I ever
did was to save the life

924
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,484
of a Valna Raider.

925
00:34:10,484 --> 00:34:12,416
You people have no respect for life.

926
00:34:12,416 --> 00:34:13,667
You'd even kill your own families

927
00:34:13,667 --> 00:34:15,267
if it brought you some advantage.

928
00:34:15,267 --> 00:34:17,250
The world will never be safe with people

929
00:34:17,250 --> 00:34:18,399
like you around.

930
00:34:18,399 --> 00:34:19,232
- [Joel] Let's kiss.

931
00:34:19,232 --> 00:34:21,697
- Look, you'd even destroy the universe.

932
00:34:21,697 --> 00:34:24,714
The minute I saw you I knew you were one

933
00:34:24,714 --> 00:34:27,086
of those savage Valna Wolves.

934
00:34:27,086 --> 00:34:29,286
- [Tom] But I love you.

935
00:34:29,286 --> 00:34:31,869
(lively music)

936
00:34:35,812 --> 00:34:37,210
- You know something?

937
00:34:37,210 --> 00:34:38,577
That was my last flight.

938
00:34:38,577 --> 00:34:39,897
I wanted to devote the rest of my life

939
00:34:39,897 --> 00:34:41,509
to my wife and kid.

940
00:34:41,509 --> 00:34:43,851
My wife just died in my arms.

941
00:34:43,851 --> 00:34:45,597
- [Crow] Hey you were
way over by the window.

942
00:34:45,597 --> 00:34:46,459
- [Tom] Yeah.

943
00:34:46,459 --> 00:34:48,667
- Honestly, where's the pride in killing

944
00:34:48,667 --> 00:34:50,869
defenseless women and children?

945
00:34:50,869 --> 00:34:52,140
You call that heroism?

946
00:34:52,140 --> 00:34:53,614
- [Crow] I call it fun.

947
00:34:53,614 --> 00:34:56,495
Don't you have any hobbies?

948
00:34:56,495 --> 00:34:58,891
- When we saved you, a
little swatch of cloth

949
00:34:58,891 --> 00:35:00,525
got torn off your uniform.

950
00:35:00,525 --> 00:35:01,523
- [Tom] Ooh.

951
00:35:01,523 --> 00:35:03,756
- I found one exactly like it.

952
00:35:03,756 --> 00:35:05,525
Next to the body of my little daughter.

953
00:35:05,525 --> 00:35:06,651
- [All] Uh-oh.

954
00:35:06,651 --> 00:35:07,650
- What have you got to say?

955
00:35:07,650 --> 00:35:09,631
- [Tom] Um oops, uh sorry?

956
00:35:09,631 --> 00:35:10,964
- I'm listening.

957
00:35:11,930 --> 00:35:14,597
(all screaming)

958
00:35:16,668 --> 00:35:18,051
- [Crow] No one can beat me at snap zooms.

959
00:35:18,051 --> 00:35:19,794
I was in Time of the Apes.

960
00:35:19,794 --> 00:35:21,860
- There's no point trying to hide it.

961
00:35:21,860 --> 00:35:23,569
I was on a mission.

962
00:35:23,569 --> 00:35:26,678
But I killed one of my
comrades in an accident.

963
00:35:26,678 --> 00:35:27,893
I ran away.

964
00:35:27,893 --> 00:35:28,726
- [Tom] Nice lips.

965
00:35:28,726 --> 00:35:31,230
- Now the other wolves
are hunting the traitor.

966
00:35:31,230 --> 00:35:33,051
- You're lying through your teeth.

967
00:35:33,051 --> 00:35:33,966
You expect me to buy that?

968
00:35:33,966 --> 00:35:35,688
- It's the truth, I swear it.

969
00:35:35,688 --> 00:35:37,311
Now listen to the rest of the story.

970
00:35:37,311 --> 00:35:39,024
- [Tom] Page two.

971
00:35:39,024 --> 00:35:40,587
- We attacked earth.

972
00:35:40,587 --> 00:35:42,305
My buddy ordered me to kill a child.

973
00:35:42,305 --> 00:35:43,975
- [Joel] They never
explain the blonde wigs.

974
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:45,092
I don't get that.

975
00:35:45,092 --> 00:35:47,669
- I couldn't and it was then
that he turned his rifle

976
00:35:47,669 --> 00:35:48,752
on the child.

977
00:35:49,868 --> 00:35:52,951
Then I saw him raise his gun to fire.

978
00:35:54,042 --> 00:35:58,231
I just wanted to get him
to put the rifle down.

979
00:35:58,231 --> 00:36:00,517
Suddenly, I looked down

980
00:36:00,517 --> 00:36:02,370
and saw that glassy look in his eyes.

981
00:36:02,370 --> 00:36:03,865
- [Tom] That sly, come-hither stare.

982
00:36:03,865 --> 00:36:06,722
- I'd forgotten how strong I was.

983
00:36:06,722 --> 00:36:08,316
- Ken, you did the right thing.

984
00:36:08,316 --> 00:36:09,149
(chanting)

985
00:36:09,149 --> 00:36:10,133
- [Joel] Now turn off the chants.

986
00:36:10,133 --> 00:36:11,100
- The world is mad.

987
00:36:11,100 --> 00:36:13,280
You know I never keep
any bullets in my gun.

988
00:36:13,280 --> 00:36:14,332
- [Crow] Like Barney Fife.

989
00:36:14,332 --> 00:36:16,947
- The thought of killing
anyone is too horrible.

990
00:36:16,947 --> 00:36:18,380
I didn't feel that way when I was

991
00:36:18,380 --> 00:36:20,316
about your age.

992
00:36:20,316 --> 00:36:22,021
I was like you, wild and reckless.

993
00:36:22,021 --> 00:36:24,162
- [Joel] That's me to a T.

994
00:36:24,162 --> 00:36:25,731
- Until today you killed for kicks.

995
00:36:25,731 --> 00:36:27,116
- [Crow] Hey like the wild rebels.

996
00:36:27,116 --> 00:36:29,578
- You were just like I used to be.

997
00:36:29,578 --> 00:36:30,411
A thrill killer.

998
00:36:30,411 --> 00:36:31,346
- I wasn't!

999
00:36:31,346 --> 00:36:32,993
I was a soldier carrying out orders.

1000
00:36:32,993 --> 00:36:34,593
There's no dishonor in that.

1001
00:36:34,593 --> 00:36:36,547
- What is dishonor then?

1002
00:36:36,547 --> 00:36:38,169
Killing for a corrupt power?

1003
00:36:38,169 --> 00:36:39,919
- [All] Punky cheeks.

1004
00:36:41,406 --> 00:36:43,656
(chanting)

1005
00:36:46,922 --> 00:36:49,505
- You betrayed us, you traitor.

1006
00:36:51,191 --> 00:36:54,619
- [Crow] See that's why
you're a scummy traitor.

1007
00:36:54,619 --> 00:36:55,452
- Cigar.

1008
00:36:55,452 --> 00:36:56,855
- [Tom] Why yes it is.

1009
00:36:56,855 --> 00:36:58,261
(Joe laughs)

1010
00:36:58,261 --> 00:37:00,818
- I've been thinking things over.

1011
00:37:00,818 --> 00:37:02,901
No point in retiring now.

1012
00:37:04,301 --> 00:37:06,836
With no wife or family to go home to.

1013
00:37:06,836 --> 00:37:07,716
- [Joel] You'll do fine.

1014
00:37:07,716 --> 00:37:11,182
- Ya know, I'm going to need
some new men in the crew.

1015
00:37:11,182 --> 00:37:13,375
- [Crow] Slim-hipped and willowy.

1016
00:37:13,375 --> 00:37:14,665
- [Tom] Big lips.

1017
00:37:14,665 --> 00:37:18,600
- Young fella who's become a fugitive.

1018
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:20,589
Who's being hunted all over the universe.

1019
00:37:20,589 --> 00:37:21,954
- [Tom] Who could that be?

1020
00:37:21,954 --> 00:37:25,021
- Could do a lot worse
than throwing in his lot

1021
00:37:25,021 --> 00:37:27,170
with the crew of Bacchus 3.

1022
00:37:27,170 --> 00:37:28,369
- [Tom] Hmmm.

1023
00:37:28,369 --> 00:37:30,267
- We might even get to be friends.

1024
00:37:30,267 --> 00:37:31,384
- [Crow] He asked me, he asked me!

1025
00:37:31,384 --> 00:37:32,558
- I don't understand.

1026
00:37:32,558 --> 00:37:34,141
What have a I done to deserve this?

1027
00:37:34,141 --> 00:37:36,184
- We don't deserve half the things we get.

1028
00:37:36,184 --> 00:37:39,184
(laughs maniacally)

1029
00:37:42,958 --> 00:37:45,007
You're stuck here.

1030
00:37:45,007 --> 00:37:45,840
Listen.

1031
00:37:45,840 --> 00:37:46,988
- [Tom] Mood swings, boy.

1032
00:37:46,988 --> 00:37:48,903
- Do exactly what I tell you

1033
00:37:48,903 --> 00:37:50,172
and you have a good chance of turning

1034
00:37:50,172 --> 00:37:52,252
into a man, not just a Wolf Raider.

1035
00:37:52,252 --> 00:37:54,209
(growling)

1036
00:37:54,209 --> 00:37:56,602
And don't you ever forget.

1037
00:37:56,602 --> 00:37:57,435
- [Tom] What?

1038
00:37:57,435 --> 00:37:58,897
- I know exactly who you
are and where you came from.

1039
00:37:58,897 --> 00:38:00,330
- [Tom] Oh.

1040
00:38:00,330 --> 00:38:02,096
- One false move and I'll set you adrift

1041
00:38:02,096 --> 00:38:04,251
to fend for yourself.

1042
00:38:04,251 --> 00:38:05,130
- [Crow] With bread crumbs.

1043
00:38:05,130 --> 00:38:06,913
- [Joel] Now let's have some fun.

1044
00:38:06,913 --> 00:38:09,349
- Now then, whether you like it or not.

1045
00:38:09,349 --> 00:38:10,394
- [Tom] She's yours.

1046
00:38:10,394 --> 00:38:12,599
- It looks like you just signed on.

1047
00:38:12,599 --> 00:38:14,211
- [Crow] Welcome to Herbal Life.

1048
00:38:14,211 --> 00:38:16,145
(dramatic music)

1049
00:38:16,145 --> 00:38:17,312
- Captain Joe.

1050
00:38:18,897 --> 00:38:20,759
(Ken laughs)

1051
00:38:20,759 --> 00:38:22,393
I kinda think I'll like it.

1052
00:38:22,393 --> 00:38:24,893
- [Crow] Yeah, whatever idiot.

1053
00:38:26,133 --> 00:38:27,425
- [Joel] Let's go skiing gang.

1054
00:38:27,425 --> 00:38:28,455
- Everything's fine.

1055
00:38:28,455 --> 00:38:31,005
(dramatic music)

1056
00:38:31,005 --> 00:38:32,461
- [Joel] In the land of Dairy Queen,

1057
00:38:32,461 --> 00:38:34,854
we treat you right.

1058
00:38:34,854 --> 00:38:36,377
- [Voiceover] While Ken was being welcomed

1059
00:38:36,377 --> 00:38:38,544
aboard Bacchus 3 and starting his life

1060
00:38:38,544 --> 00:38:40,102
as an earthling.

1061
00:38:40,102 --> 00:38:42,940
Back on Valnastar, Ken's former home,

1062
00:38:42,940 --> 00:38:44,226
the Wolf Raiders were returning

1063
00:38:44,226 --> 00:38:47,595
from their unsuccessful mission.

1064
00:38:47,595 --> 00:38:49,865
Their leader, the notorious Lord Halkun,

1065
00:38:49,865 --> 00:38:52,219
who was determined to
punish Ken mercilessly

1066
00:38:52,219 --> 00:38:53,960
for his supposed betrayal.

1067
00:38:53,960 --> 00:38:58,127
- [Tom] Meanwhile, I went
to more voiceover auditions.

1068
00:39:03,325 --> 00:39:06,888
- [Joel] Say, speak of
punishing mercilessly, whoa.

1069
00:39:06,888 --> 00:39:09,322
(whistles)

1070
00:39:09,322 --> 00:39:11,876
- [Tom] I'm wearing a
bib 'cause I just ate.

1071
00:39:11,876 --> 00:39:14,038
Tragedy tomorrow, kabuki tonight.

1072
00:39:14,038 --> 00:39:15,175
- I take it you have already heard

1073
00:39:15,175 --> 00:39:17,038
that your brother has lost his life.

1074
00:39:17,038 --> 00:39:18,004
- Yes.

1075
00:39:18,004 --> 00:39:19,404
- He was killed by Ken.

1076
00:39:19,404 --> 00:39:20,237
- Ken did it?

1077
00:39:20,237 --> 00:39:21,070
- [Tom] Those bastards.

1078
00:39:21,070 --> 00:39:22,853
- Why that can't be true.

1079
00:39:22,853 --> 00:39:24,811
- I know it must seem impossible.

1080
00:39:24,811 --> 00:39:25,644
You loved each other.

1081
00:39:25,644 --> 00:39:27,453
And he was your brother's friend.

1082
00:39:27,453 --> 00:39:29,071
I trusted him too.

1083
00:39:29,071 --> 00:39:32,371
How sad it is to put
your trust in a traitor.

1084
00:39:32,371 --> 00:39:34,001
And that's not the worst part.

1085
00:39:34,001 --> 00:39:35,756
He killed your brother in an attempt

1086
00:39:35,756 --> 00:39:36,883
to defend an earthling.

1087
00:39:36,883 --> 00:39:37,716
- [Joel] Oops.

1088
00:39:37,716 --> 00:39:38,733
- [Tom] Now we'll never
get my records back.

1089
00:39:38,733 --> 00:39:40,536
- Then he escaped into the unknown

1090
00:39:40,536 --> 00:39:41,815
in a stolen spaceship.

1091
00:39:41,815 --> 00:39:42,648
- [Joel] It'll happen.

1092
00:39:42,648 --> 00:39:44,990
- He's a coward and a traitor.

1093
00:39:44,990 --> 00:39:46,573
He has disgraced us all.

1094
00:39:46,573 --> 00:39:47,636
- [Crow] I forbid you to see him.

1095
00:39:47,636 --> 00:39:49,806
- He has forfeited the right to live.

1096
00:39:49,806 --> 00:39:51,218
- Must he die?

1097
00:39:51,218 --> 00:39:53,958
- [Halkun] Yes and you
must be his executioner.

1098
00:39:53,958 --> 00:39:56,681
It is an old Valna law that
murders must be avenged

1099
00:39:56,681 --> 00:39:58,745
by the victim's next of kin.

1100
00:39:58,745 --> 00:40:00,814
- [Tom] Not that I don't
trust you, oh wise one,

1101
00:40:00,814 --> 00:40:03,814
but can I see the book on that rule?

1102
00:40:05,556 --> 00:40:07,306
Rat Patrol, in color.

1103
00:40:12,161 --> 00:40:13,511
- [Joel] It looks like
they were shooting this

1104
00:40:13,511 --> 00:40:16,170
out of the windshield of a
Vista Cruiser station wagon.

1105
00:40:16,170 --> 00:40:19,002
- [Tom] Yeah, tinted lav.

1106
00:40:19,002 --> 00:40:21,718
- [Halkun] Ken must die by your hand.

1107
00:40:21,718 --> 00:40:24,868
You are not to return
here without his head.

1108
00:40:24,868 --> 00:40:26,317
Without his head.

1109
00:40:26,317 --> 00:40:29,553
- [Joel] Oh I gotta lay off the 'shrooms.

1110
00:40:29,553 --> 00:40:30,386
- Ken.

1111
00:40:31,305 --> 00:40:33,722
- [Crow] Did someone say Ken?

1112
00:40:35,199 --> 00:40:37,940
- Ken, you will pay
dearly for what you did.

1113
00:40:37,940 --> 00:40:39,752
- [Joel] I know, mama.

1114
00:40:39,752 --> 00:40:40,752
- [All] Huh?

1115
00:40:41,939 --> 00:40:43,153
- [Tom] Well that was easy.

1116
00:40:43,153 --> 00:40:44,789
I can go home, oh damn,
I was supposed to bring

1117
00:40:44,789 --> 00:40:46,430
back his head.

1118
00:40:46,430 --> 00:40:47,597
- [Woman] Ken!

1119
00:40:49,016 --> 00:40:51,099
- [Tom] Where aren't you?

1120
00:40:52,859 --> 00:40:55,517
- [Joel] Is she gonna need a
ride out there or somethin'?

1121
00:40:55,517 --> 00:40:56,728
- [Crow] I don't know.

1122
00:40:56,728 --> 00:41:00,645
- [Tom] You're supposed
to walk to the revenge.

1123
00:41:02,763 --> 00:41:04,400
- I know you've heard of the Star Kararu.

1124
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:06,531
It's in the center of the
seventh constellation.

1125
00:41:06,531 --> 00:41:08,764
- Inhabited by a strong
and independent nation.

1126
00:41:08,764 --> 00:41:11,014
- [Joel] The Cherokee nation.

1127
00:41:11,014 --> 00:41:13,346
- We have been aligned
with Kararu for centuries.

1128
00:41:13,346 --> 00:41:15,021
And now they are threatened.

1129
00:41:15,021 --> 00:41:17,495
Their mortal enemies have
developed a super weapon.

1130
00:41:17,495 --> 00:41:18,604
- Super weapon?

1131
00:41:18,604 --> 00:41:20,087
- [Crow] Well a really good one anyway.

1132
00:41:20,087 --> 00:41:21,228
- I don't have all the details

1133
00:41:21,228 --> 00:41:23,258
but we have an intelligence report.

1134
00:41:23,258 --> 00:41:25,841
Apparently this weapon can
destroy a whole continent.

1135
00:41:25,841 --> 00:41:27,026
If we do nothing to prevent it

1136
00:41:27,026 --> 00:41:30,341
than I'm afraid Kararu
is doomed to extinction.

1137
00:41:30,341 --> 00:41:32,725
And that is the reason that
they got in touch with us.

1138
00:41:32,725 --> 00:41:33,585
- [Tom] Now we're alone.

1139
00:41:33,585 --> 00:41:35,484
- After giving it careful consideration,

1140
00:41:35,484 --> 00:41:37,318
I've decided that you
are the only man capable

1141
00:41:37,318 --> 00:41:38,351
of doing the job.

1142
00:41:38,351 --> 00:41:40,192
- [Tom] So we're going
to get you a new dickey.

1143
00:41:40,192 --> 00:41:42,300
- But they've always
handled their own defenses.

1144
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:44,032
- This time they've got
more than one enemy.

1145
00:41:44,032 --> 00:41:44,865
- [Tom] Pool table.

1146
00:41:44,865 --> 00:41:47,813
- It looks like the Valna
Raiders are going to attack.

1147
00:41:47,813 --> 00:41:49,585
In the battle of the stars
one of the strongest forces

1148
00:41:49,585 --> 00:41:51,226
of evil in our universe.

1149
00:41:51,226 --> 00:41:52,476
- [Crow] See, what'd I tell ya?

1150
00:41:52,476 --> 00:41:54,643
(booming)

1151
00:41:56,509 --> 00:41:57,917
- [Joel] What the?

1152
00:41:57,917 --> 00:41:58,750
- [Tom] Flashback?

1153
00:41:58,750 --> 00:42:00,592
I don't know.

1154
00:42:00,592 --> 00:42:02,280
- [Crow] It's cool anyway.

1155
00:42:02,280 --> 00:42:03,239
- [Joel] Huh, I'm sorry.

1156
00:42:03,239 --> 00:42:06,913
I was just playin' a
video game in my head.

1157
00:42:06,913 --> 00:42:08,745
- I understand.

1158
00:42:08,745 --> 00:42:11,712
There's no way that they
can handle this alone.

1159
00:42:11,712 --> 00:42:15,287
- [Man] Yes, the Kararuns
are a valiant people

1160
00:42:15,287 --> 00:42:18,638
but they are no match
for the Valna Raiders.

1161
00:42:18,638 --> 00:42:19,939
- [Tom] Huh what, you were talkin' to me?

1162
00:42:19,939 --> 00:42:21,209
Oh I'm sorry, I was
thinking of the eighth hole

1163
00:42:21,209 --> 00:42:22,542
at Torrey Pines.

1164
00:42:24,752 --> 00:42:27,974
- [Joel] Let's cut the crap, I love you.

1165
00:42:27,974 --> 00:42:29,521
- I accept the mission.

1166
00:42:29,521 --> 00:42:33,385
- Good, excellent, I knew
you wouldn't disappoint us.

1167
00:42:33,385 --> 00:42:34,850
- [Joel] Yuck.

1168
00:42:34,850 --> 00:42:36,567
- [Man] I always look
forward to the crew check,

1169
00:42:36,567 --> 00:42:37,900
especially with such a fine crew

1170
00:42:37,900 --> 00:42:39,232
as the one on the Bacchus 3.

1171
00:42:39,232 --> 00:42:40,132
- [Tom] I love it.

1172
00:42:40,132 --> 00:42:40,965
- [Joe] That's Rocky.

1173
00:42:40,965 --> 00:42:42,250
- [Tom] The flying squirrel.

1174
00:42:42,250 --> 00:42:43,969
- [Joe] The best space
pilot in the business.

1175
00:42:43,969 --> 00:42:45,401
- [Joel ] And a good friend.

1176
00:42:45,401 --> 00:42:46,952
- [Joe] You remember Dan, my navigator.

1177
00:42:46,952 --> 00:42:47,831
- [Man] Indeed I do.

1178
00:42:47,831 --> 00:42:49,519
- [Tom] Ho, ho, ho, ho.

1179
00:42:49,519 --> 00:42:50,734
- [Man] Oh and this little darling

1180
00:42:50,734 --> 00:42:52,781
is your moral officer no doubt.

1181
00:42:52,781 --> 00:42:56,114
(laughing and snorting)

1182
00:42:58,867 --> 00:43:01,323
- [Joel] Doesn't sound half bad.

1183
00:43:01,323 --> 00:43:02,628
- [Man] Young Billy, he's going to make

1184
00:43:02,628 --> 00:43:03,979
a fine officer some day.

1185
00:43:03,979 --> 00:43:05,069
It's a good crew, Joe.

1186
00:43:05,069 --> 00:43:06,053
- [Joe] Not quite finished, sir.

1187
00:43:06,053 --> 00:43:09,810
- [Crow] Now I've got some
shots of the picnic here.

1188
00:43:09,810 --> 00:43:11,489
- [Tom] Who's the busboy?

1189
00:43:11,489 --> 00:43:12,322
- [Man] A new face.

1190
00:43:12,322 --> 00:43:14,614
He looks like he could
handle himself in a fight.

1191
00:43:14,614 --> 00:43:16,287
- [Joe] Oh he's rough and ready all right.

1192
00:43:16,287 --> 00:43:18,392
But that's just what I
need on this mission.

1193
00:43:18,392 --> 00:43:19,809
- A real bruiser.

1194
00:43:21,091 --> 00:43:23,515
- [Tom] Send him to my room.

1195
00:43:23,515 --> 00:43:25,740
- Listen Joe, we're asking you to set out

1196
00:43:25,740 --> 00:43:27,990
on a dangerous assignment.

1197
00:43:27,990 --> 00:43:30,497
We can't afford any unknown
quantities out there.

1198
00:43:30,497 --> 00:43:33,099
Do you know anything about
this man's background?

1199
00:43:33,099 --> 00:43:34,480
- I just wanna recruit this guy.

1200
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:35,795
- [Crow] In the worst way.

1201
00:43:35,795 --> 00:43:37,709
- I wasn't planning to adopt him.

1202
00:43:37,709 --> 00:43:39,209
- Joe, I like you.

1203
00:43:40,494 --> 00:43:41,472
- [Crow] But you're weird.

1204
00:43:41,472 --> 00:43:43,023
- Okay, if you think he's all right

1205
00:43:43,023 --> 00:43:45,053
than he's all yours.

1206
00:43:45,053 --> 00:43:47,519
- [Joel] Whoa, I'm in China, I'm in China.

1207
00:43:47,519 --> 00:43:49,186
Oh no it's just the.

1208
00:43:50,101 --> 00:43:53,536
Red ball jets help ya
run faster, jump higher.

1209
00:43:53,536 --> 00:43:54,619
- [Tom] Cool.

1210
00:43:57,849 --> 00:44:01,432
Oh, I thought I was in
a Nestea commercial.

1211
00:44:03,365 --> 00:44:05,643
- [Crow] Oh I see a bunny
and a cloud and a blonde wig

1212
00:44:05,643 --> 00:44:07,756
and a satin tap pant.

1213
00:44:07,756 --> 00:44:10,146
- [Tom] Matching camisole.

1214
00:44:10,146 --> 00:44:11,671
- [Crow] If you do it right.

1215
00:44:11,671 --> 00:44:12,504
(soft music)

1216
00:44:12,504 --> 00:44:13,999
- [Tom] Another royalty check
for Herb Alpert coming up.

1217
00:44:13,999 --> 00:44:16,749
- [Joel] Some calf muscles there.

1218
00:44:19,950 --> 00:44:21,617
I want your wig now.

1219
00:44:24,683 --> 00:44:26,996
- [Crow] It's been 26 miles.

1220
00:44:26,996 --> 00:44:28,546
It's only fun if I catch you.

1221
00:44:28,546 --> 00:44:29,379
Wait up.

1222
00:44:32,882 --> 00:44:35,730
♫ It's a tangled storm of love ♫

1223
00:44:35,730 --> 00:44:37,770
- [Joel] Come on, it's my
turn to wear the night gown.

1224
00:44:37,770 --> 00:44:39,391
- [Tom] We gotta go folks.

1225
00:44:39,391 --> 00:44:40,974
- [Crow] Let's run.

1226
00:44:42,126 --> 00:44:43,793
- Try to understand.

1227
00:44:45,292 --> 00:44:46,959
I did what I had to.

1228
00:44:47,827 --> 00:44:50,410
(lively music)

1229
00:44:54,062 --> 00:44:56,923
- Okay now Crow, I want you to be Ken.

1230
00:44:56,923 --> 00:45:00,045
And Tom I want you to be Ken.

1231
00:45:00,045 --> 00:45:01,338
- Joel, I feel ridiculous.

1232
00:45:01,338 --> 00:45:04,629
I'm dressed like Evil
Knievel only not so tasteful.

1233
00:45:04,629 --> 00:45:06,885
- Yeah Joel, I don't
wanna cast dispersions

1234
00:45:06,885 --> 00:45:08,541
on your little play-acting idea.

1235
00:45:08,541 --> 00:45:10,320
I don't wanna be the dead squirrel

1236
00:45:10,320 --> 00:45:12,321
under the floorboards
of your huntin' shack.

1237
00:45:12,321 --> 00:45:14,656
But this is the stupidest thing
you've ever had us do yet.

1238
00:45:14,656 --> 00:45:15,489
- Come on.

1239
00:45:15,489 --> 00:45:16,658
- Yeah Joe, you been
nippin' at the tester's glue

1240
00:45:16,658 --> 00:45:17,491
or what here?

1241
00:45:17,491 --> 00:45:19,039
- Come on, I just thought it would be fun

1242
00:45:19,039 --> 00:45:21,961
to play the handsome captain
of the spaceship, okay?

1243
00:45:21,961 --> 00:45:24,061
It 's a lark, a spoon,
run with me on this one.

1244
00:45:24,061 --> 00:45:26,173
I promise I'll never make ya do it again.

1245
00:45:26,173 --> 00:45:27,124
- Yeah, right.

1246
00:45:27,124 --> 00:45:29,920
Give it a week I'll have a
six-foot foam scorpion stinger

1247
00:45:29,920 --> 00:45:30,991
hanging off my butt.

1248
00:45:30,991 --> 00:45:31,824
- Come on.

1249
00:45:31,824 --> 00:45:33,401
- Look, let's just get
this over with, okay?

1250
00:45:33,401 --> 00:45:35,110
- Just come on you guys, it'll be a gas.

1251
00:45:35,110 --> 00:45:37,368
Okay, Cambot help me out on this one.

1252
00:45:37,368 --> 00:45:39,866
Neutral drive off, engines to full.

1253
00:45:39,866 --> 00:45:42,066
- All right, Ken.

1254
00:45:42,066 --> 00:45:43,968
- Now, cigar Ken?

1255
00:45:43,968 --> 00:45:44,971
- Yuck.

1256
00:45:44,971 --> 00:45:49,257
- Ya know, no sense in
me returning back home.

1257
00:45:49,257 --> 00:45:51,466
What with my wife and child gone.

1258
00:45:51,466 --> 00:45:53,731
- Oh that's right they took
a laser bolt, didn't they?

1259
00:45:53,731 --> 00:45:54,564
Too bad.

1260
00:45:54,564 --> 00:45:56,130
- Ya know, cigar Ken?

1261
00:45:56,130 --> 00:45:57,751
Ya know, a young fellow?

1262
00:45:57,751 --> 00:45:59,896
I could use a few of 'em on my ship.

1263
00:45:59,896 --> 00:46:01,316
A young fella could do a lot worse

1264
00:46:01,316 --> 00:46:04,421
than throw in with the lot of Bacchus 3.

1265
00:46:04,421 --> 00:46:06,195
We might even become friends.

1266
00:46:06,195 --> 00:46:07,101
- I don't understand.

1267
00:46:07,101 --> 00:46:08,854
What did I do to deserve this?

1268
00:46:08,854 --> 00:46:11,510
- We don't deserve half the things we get.

1269
00:46:11,510 --> 00:46:14,412
(laughs maniacally)

1270
00:46:14,412 --> 00:46:15,631
You're stuck here.

1271
00:46:15,631 --> 00:46:17,982
- Gee, Joel, don't vapor lock on us.

1272
00:46:17,982 --> 00:46:20,399
It's just a little skit
for cryin' out loud.

1273
00:46:20,399 --> 00:46:23,052
- Well so I brought
the engines to neutral.

1274
00:46:23,052 --> 00:46:24,793
- Yeah, you do exactly as I say

1275
00:46:24,793 --> 00:46:26,430
and maybe you'll find out what it means

1276
00:46:26,430 --> 00:46:30,100
to be a real man rather
than just a Wolf Raider.

1277
00:46:30,100 --> 00:46:32,033
- Yeah right and you've got a good chance

1278
00:46:32,033 --> 00:46:34,166
to end up at the Francis Farmer Motel.

1279
00:46:34,166 --> 00:46:35,562
(grunting)

1280
00:46:35,562 --> 00:46:36,988
- Jeez Joel, get a hold of yourself.

1281
00:46:36,988 --> 00:46:38,142
- Nobody hits one of my officers.

1282
00:46:38,142 --> 00:46:39,673
(alarms buzzing)

1283
00:46:39,673 --> 00:46:42,206
Oh no the movie's starting, ohhhhh.

1284
00:46:42,206 --> 00:46:44,956
(doors slamming)

1285
00:46:53,429 --> 00:46:54,634
- [Tom] I think ya broke my jaw.

1286
00:46:54,634 --> 00:46:55,713
- [Joel] Sorry 'bout that.

1287
00:46:55,713 --> 00:46:58,195
- [Tom] Jeez, outta control.

1288
00:46:58,195 --> 00:47:00,028
- [Crow] How symbolic.

1289
00:47:03,744 --> 00:47:05,135
- Are you on surveillance duty?

1290
00:47:05,135 --> 00:47:06,362
- Sorry I scared you.

1291
00:47:06,362 --> 00:47:08,827
You looked so angry I was afraid
I was gonna get strangled.

1292
00:47:08,827 --> 00:47:11,142
- [Tom] Well there's still time for that.

1293
00:47:11,142 --> 00:47:12,158
- Who's Rita?

1294
00:47:12,158 --> 00:47:13,616
Your wife or your girlfriend?

1295
00:47:13,616 --> 00:47:15,276
- [All] Yes.

1296
00:47:15,276 --> 00:47:17,240
- Cat got your tongue?

1297
00:47:17,240 --> 00:47:18,073
- [Crow] Meow.

1298
00:47:18,073 --> 00:47:18,906
- Shut up.

1299
00:47:19,872 --> 00:47:21,946
Sorry, I'm just a little tired.

1300
00:47:21,946 --> 00:47:23,558
- You know Ken, I'm beginning to think

1301
00:47:23,558 --> 00:47:25,391
you're not an earthling.

1302
00:47:25,391 --> 00:47:26,823
You haven't got the slightest idea

1303
00:47:26,823 --> 00:47:28,322
how to talk to a girl.

1304
00:47:28,322 --> 00:47:30,470
Honestly, I just wanted to say hello.

1305
00:47:30,470 --> 00:47:32,337
You didn't have to bite my head off.

1306
00:47:32,337 --> 00:47:33,422
- [Joel] Is that what I do?

1307
00:47:33,422 --> 00:47:35,378
- I don't feel like talking.

1308
00:47:35,378 --> 00:47:37,737
And I don't like people
meddling in my affairs.

1309
00:47:37,737 --> 00:47:38,936
- Oh you don't?

1310
00:47:38,936 --> 00:47:40,220
Well have it your way.

1311
00:47:40,220 --> 00:47:42,220
- [Joel] At Burger King?

1312
00:47:44,053 --> 00:47:47,043
- This crew had better
start learning to get along.

1313
00:47:47,043 --> 00:47:49,925
It's gonna be a difficult mission.

1314
00:47:49,925 --> 00:47:52,002
- [Joe] Our next mission
will take us to the Holy.

1315
00:47:52,002 --> 00:47:52,899
- [Tom] Holly Holy.

1316
00:47:52,899 --> 00:47:56,584
- However before reaching
our final destination.

1317
00:47:56,584 --> 00:47:58,804
- [Joel] We all get hats, big ones.

1318
00:47:58,804 --> 00:48:00,457
- [Tom] And scrambled eggs.

1319
00:48:00,457 --> 00:48:03,124
- As you may have heard,
Kararu and Baholee

1320
00:48:03,124 --> 00:48:04,118
are at war.

1321
00:48:04,118 --> 00:48:05,308
And recently the Wolf Raiders

1322
00:48:05,308 --> 00:48:08,184
have joined forces with Baholee.

1323
00:48:08,184 --> 00:48:09,855
In other words, this'll be no picnic.

1324
00:48:09,855 --> 00:48:11,400
- [Tom] More like a small dinner party.

1325
00:48:11,400 --> 00:48:12,989
- Well, whatta say, do we accept?

1326
00:48:12,989 --> 00:48:14,504
- Sir, I'd rather go and fight

1327
00:48:14,504 --> 00:48:17,539
than sit down here bored out of my mind.

1328
00:48:17,539 --> 00:48:19,751
- Captain, I think this is one mission

1329
00:48:19,751 --> 00:48:22,196
where you're not gonna need
whiskey for excitement.

1330
00:48:22,196 --> 00:48:23,686
(all laugh)

1331
00:48:23,686 --> 00:48:25,240
- I'll need a stiff belt
when I get back though.

1332
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:28,240
- [Crow] Ha, you'll need a big belt.

1333
00:48:29,172 --> 00:48:30,520
- [Tom] I've got baloney for arms.

1334
00:48:30,520 --> 00:48:31,846
- We're not gonna take him along.

1335
00:48:31,846 --> 00:48:33,122
- [Joe] Cool it, Danny.

1336
00:48:33,122 --> 00:48:35,496
- But Captain, who is he?

1337
00:48:35,496 --> 00:48:37,496
- I've made my decision.

1338
00:48:38,495 --> 00:48:40,162
You can take it or leave it.

1339
00:48:40,162 --> 00:48:41,027
- [Tom] Wellllll.

1340
00:48:41,027 --> 00:48:43,010
- Captain, I'm sorry.

1341
00:48:43,010 --> 00:48:44,385
I'm sure you know what you're doing.

1342
00:48:44,385 --> 00:48:45,963
(Tom laughs and snorts)

1343
00:48:45,963 --> 00:48:47,796
- Ken, welcome aboard.

1344
00:48:50,497 --> 00:48:52,284
- Are you sure you've got
what it takes for the job?

1345
00:48:52,284 --> 00:48:53,408
- You bet we have.

1346
00:48:53,408 --> 00:48:54,300
- [Tom] Don't press your luck.

1347
00:48:54,300 --> 00:48:56,476
- With Captain Joe in charge,
no mission is impossible.

1348
00:48:56,476 --> 00:48:57,975
- [Joe] Well, time will tell.

1349
00:48:57,975 --> 00:48:59,064
(lively music)

1350
00:48:59,064 --> 00:49:00,591
- [Crow] Monty Python's Flying Circus.

1351
00:49:00,591 --> 00:49:05,390
- [Joel] Hey the crew got
free tanning sessions.

1352
00:49:05,390 --> 00:49:06,223
- [Crow] Pipe down.

1353
00:49:06,223 --> 00:49:07,193
- [Tom] Pipe down please.

1354
00:49:07,193 --> 00:49:08,541
- [Joel] Pipe down please.

1355
00:49:08,541 --> 00:49:11,314
- [Tom] Pipe down please.

1356
00:49:11,314 --> 00:49:13,657
- [Tom] Huh oh, all the way down here.

1357
00:49:13,657 --> 00:49:14,490
- [Crow] Now bite me please.

1358
00:49:14,490 --> 00:49:15,876
- [Joel] Heyyyyy.

1359
00:49:15,876 --> 00:49:17,313
(lively music)

1360
00:49:17,313 --> 00:49:18,146
- [Joel] What?

1361
00:49:18,146 --> 00:49:19,038
(all laugh)

1362
00:49:19,038 --> 00:49:21,403
- Let's go fishin'.

1363
00:49:21,403 --> 00:49:23,511
- [Tom] What are Ma and Pa Kettle goin'

1364
00:49:23,511 --> 00:49:24,920
on this mission or somethin'?

1365
00:49:24,920 --> 00:49:26,341
- [Crow] Hey there's Don Knotts.

1366
00:49:26,341 --> 00:49:28,158
(Joel laughs)

1367
00:49:28,158 --> 00:49:30,205
- [Joe] I've had her
rebuilt from stem to stern.

1368
00:49:30,205 --> 00:49:31,038
- [Tom] Neat huh?

1369
00:49:31,038 --> 00:49:33,219
- [Joe] To withstand the
extreme velocities out there.

1370
00:49:33,219 --> 00:49:34,534
I don't wanna have another encounter

1371
00:49:34,534 --> 00:49:36,405
like I had with the Wolf Raiders.

1372
00:49:36,405 --> 00:49:39,139
- [Man] I thought I was
gonna explode like a balloon.

1373
00:49:39,139 --> 00:49:43,050
- [Crow] Shouldn't have
had those buffalo wings.

1374
00:49:43,050 --> 00:49:44,519
- [Man] What are the
specs on this job, sir?

1375
00:49:44,519 --> 00:49:46,249
- [Joel] Oh those are
bugs, they'll wash off.

1376
00:49:46,249 --> 00:49:47,641
- We've added a power
unit that can take us

1377
00:49:47,641 --> 00:49:50,398
up to speeds of mach 56 and over.

1378
00:49:50,398 --> 00:49:51,255
- [Crow] Yeah, pretty much.

1379
00:49:51,255 --> 00:49:52,413
- Any more speed would tear us apart.

1380
00:49:52,413 --> 00:49:53,246
- [Crow] Yeah.

1381
00:49:53,246 --> 00:49:54,079
- Ya know.

1382
00:49:54,079 --> 00:49:54,948
- [Joel] Security guard?

1383
00:49:54,948 --> 00:49:56,531
- I'm really looking
forward to flying this.

1384
00:49:56,531 --> 00:49:57,537
- So am I.

1385
00:49:57,537 --> 00:49:58,370
- [Man] Joe.

1386
00:49:58,370 --> 00:49:59,203
- Hi, Harry.

1387
00:49:59,203 --> 00:50:00,036
- [Tom] Hi teen gang.

1388
00:50:00,036 --> 00:50:01,881
- You really gonna take on that mission?

1389
00:50:01,881 --> 00:50:03,000
- Sure thing.

1390
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:04,929
- You leave the milk runs to us.

1391
00:50:04,929 --> 00:50:06,449
You always were a daredevil.

1392
00:50:06,449 --> 00:50:07,282
(both chuckle)

1393
00:50:07,282 --> 00:50:10,679
By the way, is there
any truth to that rumor?

1394
00:50:10,679 --> 00:50:12,427
They say Rocky wants out of this mission.

1395
00:50:12,427 --> 00:50:13,527
- [Tom] Come again?

1396
00:50:13,527 --> 00:50:16,360
- If he feels like a change,
I could sure use 'im.

1397
00:50:16,360 --> 00:50:18,626
- Sounds like someone's
overactive imagination.

1398
00:50:18,626 --> 00:50:21,528
Rocky's accounted for, I
wouldn't go anywhere without 'im.

1399
00:50:21,528 --> 00:50:22,559
- Right on.

1400
00:50:22,559 --> 00:50:24,142
- [Crow] Haha, you salty dog.

1401
00:50:24,142 --> 00:50:25,142
- Good luck.

1402
00:50:30,223 --> 00:50:31,876
- [Ken] This is a strange development.

1403
00:50:31,876 --> 00:50:32,762
- [Tom] Wheels everywhere.

1404
00:50:32,762 --> 00:50:35,911
- [Ken] Using my superior
strength to fight my own people.

1405
00:50:35,911 --> 00:50:37,222
- [Crow] What is this The Wonder Years?

1406
00:50:37,222 --> 00:50:39,369
- [Ken] Sure I'd love
to liberate Valnastar

1407
00:50:39,369 --> 00:50:40,667
from the tyrant Halkun.
(hissing)

1408
00:50:40,667 --> 00:50:42,338
- [Tom] Lettin' the air out of the tire.

1409
00:50:42,338 --> 00:50:45,212
- [Ken] My family's up there and Rita.

1410
00:50:45,212 --> 00:50:46,832
Does she know I killed her brother?

1411
00:50:46,832 --> 00:50:48,493
- [Joel] Maybe.

1412
00:50:48,493 --> 00:50:49,892
- [Ken] Will I ever be able to explain

1413
00:50:49,892 --> 00:50:51,879
to her what really happened.

1414
00:50:51,879 --> 00:50:53,049
- [Tom] And what about Naomi?

1415
00:50:53,049 --> 00:50:54,716
Will she love again?

1416
00:50:58,577 --> 00:50:59,914
- [Joel] Trains, neat.

1417
00:50:59,914 --> 00:51:01,500
- [Tom] Cool, big ones.

1418
00:51:01,500 --> 00:51:02,333
- [Crow] Screamers.

1419
00:51:02,333 --> 00:51:04,291
- [Ken] That guy Rocky hates me.

1420
00:51:04,291 --> 00:51:06,513
Can Captain Joe control 'im?

1421
00:51:06,513 --> 00:51:08,239
- [Tom] Or not?

1422
00:51:08,239 --> 00:51:11,906
- [Crow] Will Joe admit
that Sue loves Mary?

1423
00:51:13,654 --> 00:51:14,571
(engine growling)

1424
00:51:14,571 --> 00:51:15,757
- [Joel] A killdozer with Clint Walker.

1425
00:51:15,757 --> 00:51:16,590
Noooooo!

1426
00:51:16,590 --> 00:51:18,840
(shouting)

1427
00:51:20,245 --> 00:51:22,459
- [Crow] Eat fork, buddy.

1428
00:51:22,459 --> 00:51:25,126
- [Tom] He thinks I'm a palette.

1429
00:51:26,305 --> 00:51:27,524
- [Crow] Yeah well fortunate for me

1430
00:51:27,524 --> 00:51:30,000
I ate some more spinach
before I left the house.

1431
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:32,051
(all laughing)

1432
00:51:32,051 --> 00:51:36,218
- [Joel] Hey, come on, dim
your brights, I can't see.

1433
00:51:37,901 --> 00:51:39,865
- [Tom] Oh you should know by now pal.

1434
00:51:39,865 --> 00:51:42,619
When you push a Wolf
Raider he pushes back.

1435
00:51:42,619 --> 00:51:45,381
(laughs)

1436
00:51:45,381 --> 00:51:47,683
(grunting)

1437
00:51:47,683 --> 00:51:50,649
This must be one of
those Russian forklifts

1438
00:51:50,649 --> 00:51:53,316
I've heard so much about lately.

1439
00:51:55,879 --> 00:51:59,385
♫ This is the song written
for the train chase

1440
00:51:59,385 --> 00:52:03,311
♫ This is chase, Rocky and Ken

1441
00:52:03,311 --> 00:52:07,298
♫ He tried to kill me with a forklift

1442
00:52:07,298 --> 00:52:10,145
♫ Ole ♫

1443
00:52:10,145 --> 00:52:11,728
- [Tom] Joe Mannix!

1444
00:52:15,074 --> 00:52:15,907
- Rocky?

1445
00:52:15,907 --> 00:52:17,134
- [Crow] Again.

1446
00:52:17,134 --> 00:52:18,642
- Well that answers my question.

1447
00:52:18,642 --> 00:52:19,686
- [Tom] What was the question?

1448
00:52:19,686 --> 00:52:22,240
- I thought you were a Wolf Raider.

1449
00:52:22,240 --> 00:52:24,608
They planted you on our flight
to sabotage our mission.

1450
00:52:24,608 --> 00:52:25,959
- [Joel] Yeah well you're a wuss raider.

1451
00:52:25,959 --> 00:52:27,209
- [Tom] Wooooo!

1452
00:52:31,095 --> 00:52:31,928
- [Joel] What are you doing?

1453
00:52:31,928 --> 00:52:32,802
Are you high?

1454
00:52:32,802 --> 00:52:34,819
I have the strength of 20 men.

1455
00:52:34,819 --> 00:52:38,600
♫ This is the song right
after the train chase

1456
00:52:38,600 --> 00:52:42,717
♫ This is the fight, Rocky and Ken ♫

1457
00:52:42,717 --> 00:52:43,550
- [Crow] Again?

1458
00:52:43,550 --> 00:52:44,634
- What's going on?

1459
00:52:44,634 --> 00:52:46,500
- [Joel] Um, nothing sir.

1460
00:52:46,500 --> 00:52:47,874
- Captain!

1461
00:52:47,874 --> 00:52:48,717
- [Crow] Hazing the freshman.

1462
00:52:48,717 --> 00:52:51,684
- [Tom] I told you no
grabass in the shower.

1463
00:52:51,684 --> 00:52:52,981
- I know who he is now.

1464
00:52:52,981 --> 00:52:54,631
- [Crow] He's my mother, he's my sister.

1465
00:52:54,631 --> 00:52:57,514
He's my mother and my sister.

1466
00:52:57,514 --> 00:53:01,681
♫ He tried to kill me with a forklift ♫

1467
00:53:02,803 --> 00:53:04,334
- Rocky, how often do I have to tell you

1468
00:53:04,334 --> 00:53:06,480
you should stop reading
those science fiction novels?

1469
00:53:06,480 --> 00:53:09,531
- [Crow] They're comic books.

1470
00:53:09,531 --> 00:53:12,106
- I know Ken's a lot stronger than we are.

1471
00:53:12,106 --> 00:53:14,499
There's a reasonable scientific
explanation for that.

1472
00:53:14,499 --> 00:53:16,880
He spent a lot of time
in another constellation.

1473
00:53:16,880 --> 00:53:19,604
That increases strength.

1474
00:53:19,604 --> 00:53:23,771
- [Joel] You are a liar I
don't believe just like him.

1475
00:53:25,523 --> 00:53:27,048
- Don't expect any gratitude from me.

1476
00:53:27,048 --> 00:53:28,317
- [Tom] Okay.

1477
00:53:28,317 --> 00:53:29,150
- I won't.

1478
00:53:30,849 --> 00:53:31,948
Now you listen to this.

1479
00:53:31,948 --> 00:53:33,398
- [Crow] Pull my finger.

1480
00:53:33,398 --> 00:53:35,764
- What I expect from
you is total obedience.

1481
00:53:35,764 --> 00:53:37,159
- [Tom] If that's okay with you.

1482
00:53:37,159 --> 00:53:38,502
- Ya know you'll only continue to live

1483
00:53:38,502 --> 00:53:40,820
as long as I shut up.

1484
00:53:40,820 --> 00:53:43,570
(dramatic music)

1485
00:53:50,035 --> 00:53:51,368
- [Ken] Shut up.

1486
00:53:52,711 --> 00:53:53,794
- [Crow] Wow.

1487
00:53:56,480 --> 00:53:58,647
- [Joel] Oooh, Aaah, Oooh.

1488
00:53:59,956 --> 00:54:02,103
- [Crow] Gah it's so great.

1489
00:54:02,103 --> 00:54:03,263
It's only a model.

1490
00:54:03,263 --> 00:54:05,218
- [Tom] All right, spit
out the sunflower seeds.

1491
00:54:05,218 --> 00:54:06,768
- [Voiceover] And so, our
valiant space adventurers

1492
00:54:06,768 --> 00:54:10,101
prepared to embark on a
perilous and exciting mission.

1493
00:54:10,101 --> 00:54:13,601
- [Joel] Hold the ship, lose the building.

1494
00:54:14,653 --> 00:54:17,820
- [Voiceover] Meanwhile, on Valnastar.

1495
00:54:18,911 --> 00:54:20,049
- [Tom] Say.

1496
00:54:20,049 --> 00:54:21,424
- [Voiceover] Other plans are being made.

1497
00:54:21,424 --> 00:54:22,257
- [Halkun] Remember Rita, it is our law.

1498
00:54:22,257 --> 00:54:25,070
You may not return until.

1499
00:54:25,070 --> 00:54:27,070
- [Joel] Mayan drawings?

1500
00:54:32,373 --> 00:54:34,414
- [Tom] Tell me spirit, are these shadows

1501
00:54:34,414 --> 00:54:38,364
of things which must be or which might be?

1502
00:54:38,364 --> 00:54:41,114
(birds chirping)

1503
00:54:41,964 --> 00:54:44,214
(mumbling)

1504
00:54:47,574 --> 00:54:49,510
- [Tom] Hey look, 27 8x10
colored glossy pictures

1505
00:54:49,510 --> 00:54:50,856
with the circles and
arrows and the paragraph

1506
00:54:50,856 --> 00:54:52,225
on the back of each one.

1507
00:54:52,225 --> 00:54:54,822
- [Crow] Why am I thinking
of the cast party now?

1508
00:54:54,822 --> 00:54:56,405
Oh I like that one.

1509
00:54:58,818 --> 00:55:01,422
- [Joel] Uh, that'll be
53 bucks for the photos.

1510
00:55:01,422 --> 00:55:02,255
- Barbara.

1511
00:55:03,120 --> 00:55:05,018
- [Tom] Whose hand is that?

1512
00:55:05,018 --> 00:55:06,116
- [Crow] I can be Barbara.

1513
00:55:06,116 --> 00:55:07,699
- My baby, my wife.

1514
00:55:08,733 --> 00:55:09,566
- [Crow] Whatever.

1515
00:55:09,566 --> 00:55:10,933
- I don't care anymore what happens to me

1516
00:55:10,933 --> 00:55:12,683
out beyond the stars.

1517
00:55:14,538 --> 00:55:17,843
If I don't survive, then
we can be together again

1518
00:55:17,843 --> 00:55:20,020
that much sooner.

1519
00:55:20,020 --> 00:55:22,894
- [Joel] Oh would somebody
turn the fryer light off me.

1520
00:55:22,894 --> 00:55:25,311
- Rest peacefully until then.

1521
00:55:26,967 --> 00:55:28,978
It won't be long now.

1522
00:55:28,978 --> 00:55:30,714
- [Tom] What a sap.

1523
00:55:30,714 --> 00:55:33,676
(soft music)

1524
00:55:33,676 --> 00:55:36,295
- [Joel] Oh I've got the
wrong grave, I'm sorry.

1525
00:55:36,295 --> 00:55:37,462
- [Crow] Olga?

1526
00:55:38,477 --> 00:55:40,245
- [Tom] Oh it's embarrassing.

1527
00:55:40,245 --> 00:55:44,229
- [Joel] Um, I gotta go
paint a house now, sorry.

1528
00:55:44,229 --> 00:55:46,442
- [Crow] Hey they're
havin' a jumpsuit party.

1529
00:55:46,442 --> 00:55:48,613
His is the grandest of all.

1530
00:55:48,613 --> 00:55:50,941
- Thanks, you're a great crew.

1531
00:55:50,941 --> 00:55:54,711
- [Joel] Read to levitate the table?

1532
00:55:54,711 --> 00:55:55,811
- To the mission.

1533
00:55:55,811 --> 00:55:57,424
- [All] Cheers!

1534
00:55:57,424 --> 00:56:00,313
- [Tammy] Rocky, aren't
you going to drink with us?

1535
00:56:00,313 --> 00:56:02,064
- [Tom] Gonna fly now?

1536
00:56:02,064 --> 00:56:03,564
