01:23:59,815 --> 01:24:01,407
- [Joel] Die, Joel.

2293
01:24:01,407 --> 01:24:02,273
- [Tom] Huh?

2294
01:24:02,273 --> 01:24:04,523
- [All] Button bombs, whoa!

2295
01:24:06,070 --> 01:24:08,313
- [Crow] Hey wow, those
things really work.

2296
01:24:08,313 --> 01:24:09,436
- [Joel] Ya gotta
remember to take them off

2297
01:24:09,436 --> 01:24:11,273
before you take your
clothes to the laundry.

2298
01:24:11,273 --> 01:24:12,609
- [Crow] Oh yeah.

2299
01:24:12,609 --> 01:24:14,410
- [Tom] Blow up a dry cleaner.

2300
01:24:14,410 --> 01:24:17,327
Oh this was a good plan, wasn't it?

2301
01:24:20,941 --> 01:24:21,774
Whoops.

2302
01:24:23,226 --> 01:24:24,158
All right, come on in.

2303
01:24:24,158 --> 01:24:24,991
Bring 'er down.

2304
01:24:24,991 --> 01:24:25,994
Uh, little right, little right.

2305
01:24:25,994 --> 01:24:28,092
Up there ya go, watch your space cushion.

2306
01:24:28,092 --> 01:24:29,990
It's a little driving joke.

2307
01:24:29,990 --> 01:24:32,227
Bring it down, keep
going, come on, come on.

2308
01:24:32,227 --> 01:24:33,460
- [Crow] No, I'm sorry
you failed your test.

2309
01:24:33,460 --> 01:24:35,274
You'll have to come back in two weeks.

2310
01:24:35,274 --> 01:24:37,607
Happens to most of the guys.

2311
01:24:39,263 --> 01:24:40,101
- This is Joe.

2312
01:24:40,101 --> 01:24:41,638
- [Joel] Hello Joe, whatta ya know?

2313
01:24:41,638 --> 01:24:44,379
- [Tom] Just got back from Kokomo.

2314
01:24:44,379 --> 01:24:45,212
- Ken?

2315
01:24:46,142 --> 01:24:46,975
- [Tom] Ken?

2316
01:24:46,975 --> 01:24:47,808
- Can ya hear me?

2317
01:24:47,808 --> 01:24:49,475
Ken, please come in.

2318
01:24:50,630 --> 01:24:52,188
- [Tom] Ready?

2319
01:24:52,188 --> 01:24:55,418
♫ I love Ken and a guy named Ken

2320
01:24:55,418 --> 01:24:59,452
♫ And I fell in love with a guy named Ken

2321
01:24:59,452 --> 01:25:03,294
♫ I'm in love with a guy named Ken

2322
01:25:03,294 --> 01:25:05,228
♫ And it hurts me so

2323
01:25:05,228 --> 01:25:07,495
♫ And it hurts me so

2324
01:25:07,495 --> 01:25:11,069
♫ And it hurts me soooooo ♫

2325
01:25:11,069 --> 01:25:12,561
- [Joel] Moses?

2326
01:25:12,561 --> 01:25:13,476
- [Ken] Arita.

2327
01:25:13,476 --> 01:25:14,408
- [Crow] Meeta maid.

2328
01:25:14,408 --> 01:25:16,208
Where would I be without you.

2329
01:25:16,208 --> 01:25:17,573
- I'm seeing things.

2330
01:25:17,573 --> 01:25:18,739
- [Joel] No, you're seeing me.

2331
01:25:18,739 --> 01:25:20,037
Is that what I am to you, a thing?

2332
01:25:20,037 --> 01:25:22,708
- This must be a hallucination.

2333
01:25:22,708 --> 01:25:24,165
- [Crow] With that hair it must be.

2334
01:25:24,165 --> 01:25:25,199
- [Tom] Mmm-hmm.

2335
01:25:25,199 --> 01:25:26,032
- Rita!

2336
01:25:26,932 --> 01:25:28,682
What are you doing here?

2337
01:25:28,682 --> 01:25:30,513
- I've been trying to
track you down for days.

2338
01:25:30,513 --> 01:25:32,854
We got a radio message that you'd broken

2339
01:25:32,854 --> 01:25:34,697
out of a Kararu jail.

2340
01:25:34,697 --> 01:25:37,197
They said you were a traitor.

2341
01:25:37,197 --> 01:25:40,428
And here you are in an
Earth Space Command uniform.

2342
01:25:40,428 --> 01:25:41,529
- [Tom] Traiting.

2343
01:25:41,529 --> 01:25:43,779
- I was forced to wear this uniform.

2344
01:25:43,779 --> 01:25:45,828
They said they'd kill me otherwise.

2345
01:25:45,828 --> 01:25:47,348
- A likely story.

2346
01:25:47,348 --> 01:25:49,280
I don't know what's come over you, Ken.

2347
01:25:49,280 --> 01:25:50,560
- [Crow] I want my tapes back.

2348
01:25:50,560 --> 01:25:51,879
- You've turned traitor.

2349
01:25:51,879 --> 01:25:53,388
Abandoned me and killed my brother.

2350
01:25:53,388 --> 01:25:54,998
- It was an accident.

2351
01:25:54,998 --> 01:25:56,114
- [Tom] Okay.

2352
01:25:56,114 --> 01:25:57,857
- He was getting ready
to shoot a little boy

2353
01:25:57,857 --> 01:25:59,607
whose name also happened to be Ken.

2354
01:25:59,607 --> 01:26:01,441
I was just trying to stop him.

2355
01:26:01,441 --> 01:26:02,305
- [Woman] Ken!

2356
01:26:02,305 --> 01:26:05,188
- [Tom] But we'll just run the clip.

2357
01:26:05,188 --> 01:26:06,474
- Don't shoot!

2358
01:26:06,474 --> 01:26:09,946
- [Crow] Oh come on, we're
intimate with this scene

2359
01:26:09,946 --> 01:26:10,975
for crying out loud.

2360
01:26:10,975 --> 01:26:12,495
- Traitor.

2361
01:26:12,495 --> 01:26:14,020
- That's what really happened, Rita.

2362
01:26:14,020 --> 01:26:16,181
I swear I'm telling you the truth.

2363
01:26:16,181 --> 01:26:18,136
I'm not a traitor to our country.

2364
01:26:18,136 --> 01:26:20,073
You know that, I simply refused

2365
01:26:20,073 --> 01:26:22,485
to kill an innocent child.

2366
01:26:22,485 --> 01:26:24,502
And I didn't wanna
fight with your brother.

2367
01:26:24,502 --> 01:26:25,351
- [Joel] So I killed 'im.

2368
01:26:25,351 --> 01:26:26,835
- [Rita] I believe you.

2369
01:26:26,835 --> 01:26:29,192
You can't betray a country
you never belonged to.

2370
01:26:29,192 --> 01:26:30,153
- [Tom] Huh?

2371
01:26:30,153 --> 01:26:31,972
- [Rita] Ken you once told
me your father came to Valna

2372
01:26:31,972 --> 01:26:33,207
as a missionary.

2373
01:26:33,207 --> 01:26:34,144
- [Tom] Oh that bag,
I thought they cleared

2374
01:26:34,144 --> 01:26:35,324
that up in counseling.

2375
01:26:35,324 --> 01:26:36,157
- [Rita] You're really an earthling.

2376
01:26:36,157 --> 01:26:39,129
- Go on, go on, murder me in cold blood

2377
01:26:39,129 --> 01:26:40,138
if you want to.

2378
01:26:40,138 --> 01:26:41,404
- You deserve worse.

2379
01:26:41,404 --> 01:26:42,874
To die a slow death.

2380
01:26:42,874 --> 01:26:44,179
- Then what are you waiting for?

2381
01:26:44,179 --> 01:26:46,130
I know Valna law as well as you do.

2382
01:26:46,130 --> 01:26:47,663
I caused your brother's death

2383
01:26:47,663 --> 01:26:49,992
and now you've been sent out to kill me.

2384
01:26:49,992 --> 01:26:52,391
Well I'm all ready to die, Rita.

2385
01:26:52,391 --> 01:26:53,576
- Ken.

2386
01:26:53,576 --> 01:26:55,495
- You'd be doing me a favor.

2387
01:26:55,495 --> 01:26:57,147
I can't live in dishonor.

2388
01:26:57,147 --> 01:26:58,480
Go ahead, shoot.

2389
01:26:59,624 --> 01:27:02,161
- [Crow] But first,
swallow my lapel button.

2390
01:27:02,161 --> 01:27:04,389
As a symbol of our love, hmmm?

2391
01:27:04,389 --> 01:27:06,989
- [Tom] Shoot him down, shoot to kill.

2392
01:27:06,989 --> 01:27:08,406
- [Joel] Stinker.

2393
01:27:10,186 --> 01:27:11,769
- [Tom] Buck fever.

2394
01:27:12,821 --> 01:27:15,485
Oh it's made out of electrician's tape.

2395
01:27:15,485 --> 01:27:17,570
- [Ken] Come on, get it over with.

2396
01:27:17,570 --> 01:27:19,123
What's the point of
living if the girl I love

2397
01:27:19,123 --> 01:27:21,752
more than life itself
thinks that I'm a traitor?

2398
01:27:21,752 --> 01:27:22,585
- [Joel] Kill him.

2399
01:27:22,585 --> 01:27:23,418
- [Tom] Kill him.

2400
01:27:23,418 --> 01:27:24,418
- Now, Rita.

2401
01:27:26,339 --> 01:27:28,271
- [Crow] Hey ya know this
is just like Richard III.

2402
01:27:28,271 --> 01:27:30,366
- [Tom] Sure is.

2403
01:27:30,366 --> 01:27:31,434
(Rita sobs)

2404
01:27:31,434 --> 01:27:32,267
Won't do it.

2405
01:27:32,267 --> 01:27:33,634
- [Joel] It took me seven
days to get this gun

2406
01:27:33,634 --> 01:27:35,217
now I can't use it.

2407
01:27:39,366 --> 01:27:42,998
- [Tom] Nice to see there
was a damn in the background.

2408
01:27:42,998 --> 01:27:47,144
- [Joel] That peasant
blouse is all wrong on her.

2409
01:27:47,144 --> 01:27:48,660
- I can't do it.

2410
01:27:48,660 --> 01:27:50,504
I can't kill the man I love.

2411
01:27:50,504 --> 01:27:53,754
- [Crow] Then kill the one you're with.

2412
01:27:55,384 --> 01:27:56,787
- Oh my foot!

2413
01:27:56,787 --> 01:28:00,221
Why am I having such a crappy day?

2414
01:28:00,221 --> 01:28:01,302
- Rita.

2415
01:28:01,302 --> 01:28:02,885
- [All] Meeta Maid.

2416
01:28:05,486 --> 01:28:07,544
- [Tom] Glycerin tear again.

2417
01:28:07,544 --> 01:28:09,044
- My darling, Ken.

2418
01:28:11,615 --> 01:28:13,384
- [Tom] I'm gonna have
to remember that line

2419
01:28:13,384 --> 01:28:15,301
for the bars, it works.

2420
01:28:16,323 --> 01:28:20,120
- [Crow] Um, you're crying on my bomb.

2421
01:28:20,120 --> 01:28:21,203
- [Tom] Ouch.

2422
01:28:22,863 --> 01:28:23,902
- Rita.

2423
01:28:23,902 --> 01:28:26,985
- [Joel] Oh get off the tilt-a-whirl.

2424
01:28:29,209 --> 01:28:31,538
- [Tom] Oh it's over.

2425
01:28:31,538 --> 01:28:32,994
- [Crow] That was great.

2426
01:28:32,994 --> 01:28:33,846
- What happens to us now?

2427
01:28:33,846 --> 01:28:36,567
Are we both just fugitives in space?

2428
01:28:36,567 --> 01:28:38,329
No matter what you or I say or do,

2429
01:28:38,329 --> 01:28:40,148
they'll never let us go home.

2430
01:28:40,148 --> 01:28:43,087
Valna, I'd love to see it again.

2431
01:28:43,087 --> 01:28:44,775
- What do we need Valna for?

2432
01:28:44,775 --> 01:28:46,009
We've got each other.

2433
01:28:46,009 --> 01:28:47,942
We can start a new life somewhere else.

2434
01:28:47,942 --> 01:28:49,459
- [Tom] On a slag heap?

2435
01:28:49,459 --> 01:28:51,108
- Rita, it won't work.

2436
01:28:51,108 --> 01:28:53,391
They'll never leave us
in peace, you know that.

2437
01:28:53,391 --> 01:28:55,749
- How can you say that.

2438
01:28:55,749 --> 01:28:58,856
If we keep loving each
other, we'll find a way.

2439
01:28:58,856 --> 01:29:00,022
- [Joel] Boy you are naive.

2440
01:29:00,022 --> 01:29:01,405
- How long can that love last?

2441
01:29:01,405 --> 01:29:02,605
You know what you'll see every morning

2442
01:29:02,605 --> 01:29:03,944
when you wake up?

2443
01:29:03,944 --> 01:29:05,359
You'll be staring straight at the man

2444
01:29:05,359 --> 01:29:06,640
who killed your brother.

2445
01:29:06,640 --> 01:29:07,638
- [Crow] Will you be there too?

2446
01:29:07,638 --> 01:29:08,811
- Ken.

2447
01:29:08,811 --> 01:29:09,937
- It won't work, Rita.

2448
01:29:09,937 --> 01:29:12,492
Too much has already happened to us.

2449
01:29:12,492 --> 01:29:14,604
Soon we'd start hating each other.

2450
01:29:14,604 --> 01:29:16,112
- I won't let you talk like that.

2451
01:29:16,112 --> 01:29:17,725
- It just won't work.

2452
01:29:17,725 --> 01:29:18,986
Why didn't you kill me before?

2453
01:29:18,986 --> 01:29:19,819
- What?

2454
01:29:20,689 --> 01:29:21,952
- You heard.

2455
01:29:21,952 --> 01:29:23,485
Kill me and get it over with.

2456
01:29:23,485 --> 01:29:25,439
- [Tom] Come on chicken, you
chicken, come on kill me,

2457
01:29:25,439 --> 01:29:27,735
come on chicken (clucking)

2458
01:29:27,735 --> 01:29:30,902
- [Joel] I wonder what he's thinking.

2459
01:29:30,902 --> 01:29:33,152
- [Crow] Ditch 'er, go run.

2460
01:29:34,399 --> 01:29:37,606
- [Tom] You are going to die.

2461
01:29:37,606 --> 01:29:38,552
I am going to kill you.

2462
01:29:38,552 --> 01:29:39,385
- Ken.

2463
01:29:43,725 --> 01:29:44,642
[Tom] Rita.

2464
01:29:46,857 --> 01:29:49,203
(soldier screams)

2465
01:29:49,203 --> 01:29:50,873
He killed the tree.

2466
01:29:50,873 --> 01:29:52,263
(weapons firing)

2467
01:29:52,263 --> 01:29:54,680
(Ken groans)

2468
01:29:57,963 --> 01:29:58,796
- Rita!

2469
01:29:58,796 --> 01:30:00,165
- [All] Meeta maid!

2470
01:30:00,165 --> 01:30:02,916
- Rita, are you all right?

2471
01:30:02,916 --> 01:30:05,113
- [Crow] I killed your
other brothers by the way.

2472
01:30:05,113 --> 01:30:09,030
- Ken, traitor, it was
you who fired that shot.

2473
01:30:11,177 --> 01:30:12,094
It was you.

2474
01:30:14,316 --> 01:30:15,677
- [Joel] Wait, let me explain.

2475
01:30:15,677 --> 01:30:16,510
Oh darn.

2476
01:30:19,744 --> 01:30:23,866
- [Ken] The most important
part of me just died too.

2477
01:30:23,866 --> 01:30:24,815
- [Crow] Well at least he gets to keep

2478
01:30:24,815 --> 01:30:27,684
that swell Star Trek stuff.

2479
01:30:27,684 --> 01:30:30,555
- [Tom] Well honey, looks like
I'm gonna have to gut 'ya.

2480
01:30:30,555 --> 01:30:32,046
- [Joel And Crow] Ohhhhhh.

2481
01:30:32,046 --> 01:30:34,852
- [Joel] That's it, make
it look like a robbery.

2482
01:30:34,852 --> 01:30:35,975
- I heard gunfire.

2483
01:30:35,975 --> 01:30:36,808
Are you all right?

2484
01:30:36,808 --> 01:30:37,800
- [Crow] Where have you been?

2485
01:30:37,800 --> 01:30:40,888
- I'm fine, the others are dead.

2486
01:30:40,888 --> 01:30:42,781
- Who's she, what happened to her?

2487
01:30:42,781 --> 01:30:45,186
- A Kararun girl got
caught in the crossfire.

2488
01:30:45,186 --> 01:30:46,224
- [Crow] Huh, bummer.

2489
01:30:46,224 --> 01:30:47,766
- It's late, we better get going.

2490
01:30:47,766 --> 01:30:49,402
There's nothing we can do here.

2491
01:30:49,402 --> 01:30:50,656
- [Tom] But I'm thirsty again.

2492
01:30:50,656 --> 01:30:53,164
- [Crow] Will you get going?

2493
01:30:53,164 --> 01:30:55,914
- [Ken] Good-bye, Rita, good-bye.

2494
01:30:56,870 --> 01:30:58,688
- [Joel] Come back, I'm not dead.

2495
01:30:58,688 --> 01:31:01,105
You didn't check for a pulse.

2496
01:31:09,161 --> 01:31:11,911
- [Crow] Next time on Twin Peaks.

2497
01:31:13,443 --> 01:31:14,774
- Help, Ken.

2498
01:31:14,774 --> 01:31:16,024
- I've got you.

2499
01:31:18,765 --> 01:31:21,560
- [Tom] Come 'ere you, come on.

2500
01:31:21,560 --> 01:31:23,098
- [Joel] Let 'im go.

2501
01:31:23,098 --> 01:31:24,657
Drop 'im.

2502
01:31:24,657 --> 01:31:27,106
- [Tom] Would you take those
rocks out of your pockets.

2503
01:31:27,106 --> 01:31:28,045
- [Crow] Rock climbing, Joel.

2504
01:31:28,045 --> 01:31:29,878
- [Tom] Rock climbing.

2505
01:31:35,048 --> 01:31:36,559
- [Crow] Casesar Romero?

2506
01:31:36,559 --> 01:31:37,809
Edmund Hillary?

2507
01:31:39,807 --> 01:31:40,954
- [Joel] Oh they're down there.

2508
01:31:40,954 --> 01:31:41,954
Jump for it!

2509
01:31:43,660 --> 01:31:44,660
- Hey-ey-ey!

2510
01:31:46,561 --> 01:31:49,561
(imitating gunfire)

2511
01:31:55,556 --> 01:31:57,235
- [Joel] New from the Franklin Mint.

2512
01:31:57,235 --> 01:31:58,759
- [Crow] Oh, he's sendin' 'em a message.

2513
01:31:58,759 --> 01:32:01,250
He's saying, hey my emblem came off.

2514
01:32:01,250 --> 01:32:03,067
(dramatic music)

2515
01:32:03,067 --> 01:32:04,451
- [Tom] Do do do.

2516
01:32:04,451 --> 01:32:06,152
♫ Ken and his friend are free

2517
01:32:06,152 --> 01:32:08,186
♫ Their free together

2518
01:32:08,186 --> 01:32:10,131
♫ Ken and his friend are free

2519
01:32:10,131 --> 01:32:11,874
♫ They're free to be you and me ♫

2520
01:32:11,874 --> 01:32:15,124
- [Crow] I'm blind, I'm blind, help me.

2521
01:32:16,621 --> 01:32:17,891
- Ho-ho-ho!

2522
01:32:17,891 --> 01:32:19,854
- [Tom] Take a picture
of us, we're posing.

2523
01:32:19,854 --> 01:32:20,887
- [Crow] It'll last longer.

2524
01:32:20,887 --> 01:32:21,720
- Ken!

2525
01:32:21,720 --> 01:32:23,045
- [Tom] Nice teeth.

2526
01:32:23,045 --> 01:32:24,575
- Captain, Ken made it.

2527
01:32:24,575 --> 01:32:25,770
- [Joel] Captain Ken made it?

2528
01:32:25,770 --> 01:32:27,086
- What about the Caesar officer?

2529
01:32:27,086 --> 01:32:28,393
- He's there too.

2530
01:32:28,393 --> 01:32:29,620
- I knew he'd pull it off.

2531
01:32:29,620 --> 01:32:30,944
- [Crow] Now let's break out the liquor.

2532
01:32:30,944 --> 01:32:32,444
Oh I drank it all.

2533
01:32:33,302 --> 01:32:34,402
- [Man] Ken you did it.

2534
01:32:34,402 --> 01:32:35,235
- [Tammy] Ken!

2535
01:32:35,235 --> 01:32:36,068
- [Joe] Good work, son.

2536
01:32:36,068 --> 01:32:37,119
- [Man] Welcome back, Ken.

2537
01:32:37,119 --> 01:32:37,952
- [Tammy] I was so worried about you.

2538
01:32:37,952 --> 01:32:39,376
Oh Ken!

2539
01:32:39,376 --> 01:32:42,217
(throat clearing)

2540
01:32:42,217 --> 01:32:43,784
- [Officer] Let me introduce myself.

2541
01:32:43,784 --> 01:32:44,884
- [Tom] I'm a man of wealth and taste.

2542
01:32:44,884 --> 01:32:46,801
- Sir, welcome Colonel.

2543
01:32:48,018 --> 01:32:49,871
I'm Captain Joe, welcome aboard.

2544
01:32:49,871 --> 01:32:52,667
- [Joel] This is my fleet
of Elvis impersonators.

2545
01:32:52,667 --> 01:32:56,334
